WEBVTT

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.240
Mom?!

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.630
Stay away, Ran!

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.520
Just a dream...

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:12.820
Eh? You dreamed I was shot?

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.820
Is that why you called me so early in the morning?

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.700
Oh, come on, I was worried!

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.620
Sometimes even lawyers get people who have grudges against them...

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:27.500
You're just being paranoid, Ran.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.500
It's because of all those crimes you've seen

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.300
that you have dreams like that.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.840
But I'm glad you're all right!

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:41.430
Oh, yeah! You were a little younger in my dream, you know!

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:48.480
My! How rude! I'll have you know I'm <i>still</i> young!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:54.900
Oh, I'm sorry! Please forgive my rudeness!

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.740
Very well, then!

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.490
Okay, so 7:00 tonight, right?
Dad and Conan-<i>Kun</i> can't wait, either!

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:18.800
I wonder... Does she remember?

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.390
Conan-<i>kun...</i>

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:31.980
What's goin' on? Why're you up so early?

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:37.360
Oh, no reason. Sorry for waking you up.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:41.990
Oh, it's tonight! Our dinner date with Ran's mom...

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:44.950
Man, I can't stand that lady...

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.720
<i>I'm high school detective Kudo Shinichi.</i>

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.810
<i>I went with old friend and classmate,</i>
<i>Mori Ran, to an amusement park</i>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:11.400
<i>where I witnessed a suspicious deal</i> <i>with a man dressed in black!</i>

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.900
<i>I was so absorbed with watching the deal</i>

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.030
<i>that I didn't notice a second man</i> <i>sneak up from behind me!</i>

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.740
<i>He forced me to take a poison,</i> <i>and when I woke up...</i>

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:26.990
<i>...my body had shrunk!</i>

00:03:26.990 --> 00:03:30.960
<i>If they learned Kudo Shinichi was alive,</i> <i>they might go after me again,</i>

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.880
<i>putting all the people around me in danger!</i>

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:37.500
<i>Per Dr. Agasa's advice,</i>
<i>I decided to conceal my identity.</i>

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:42.050
<i>When Ran asked my name,</i>
<i>I quickly answered, "Edogawa Conan."</i>

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.840
<i>To get information on the men,</i>

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.510
<i>I wound up living with Ran</i> <i>and her detective father.</i>

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:51.640
<i>Yes. This guy is Ran's father...</i>

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:56.980
<i>...and the now-incredibly famous detective, Mori Kogoro.</i>

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.860
<i>But he's really a bonehead detective...</i>

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:03.360
<i>...and you all know who's really solving the crimes, right?</i>

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:09.080
The secret behind that is in the two gadgets Dr. Agasa made for me!

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:13.620
The first... is this!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.580
The Stun-Gun Wrist-Watch!

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.550
Pressing the button while using the aiming device on the cover

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:25.970
will launch a tranquilizer needle that can knock a person out instantly!

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.270
Next is the Voice-Changing Bow-Tie!

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.980
By adjusting the dials on the back,

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:36.190
I can produce all types of voices, from children to adult!

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:40.780
For offensive items, I have the Power Assisted Kick Shoes!

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.860
They use electricity and magnetic fields to stimulate my feet muscles

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.950
and maximize my kick power!

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.700
To chase down criminals, I have the Turbo-Engine Skateboard!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.380
And an unexpectedly sweet item are these Elasticity Suspenders!

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:03.470
One press of a button, and the rubber will expand or contract!

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.810
It's a really unique gadget!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:24.240
I can't ID the men in black yet, but other cases won't wait for me!

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.530
Even when I'm small, my mind remains that of a sharp detective!

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:30.240
There is always only one truth!

00:05:57.350 --> 00:05:58.560
"Mori Kogoro - Beika Street, Beika City"

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.200
Genta-<i>kun</i>! You're gonna eat that one, too?!

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.120
Who cares how many I eat?!

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:17.080
This one's a Black Choco Bar!
It's got a grownup taste!

00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:19.080
Oh?! Really?!

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.580
Yeah, right.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.800
Geez, what's taking him so long?

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:34.930
Look! Look!

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.600
Conan-<i>Kun</i> and I are a perfect match!

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.850
"You two are a perfect match!"

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.440
A-are you sure that game's not broken?!

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.190
B-but more importantly, Genta-<i>kun</i>!

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:48.240
Card fortune-telling is obviously a pack of lies!

00:06:51.160 --> 00:06:54.620
Now let's check Conan-<i>kun</i>'s!
His birthday is...

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:55.950
Hey, now.

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:59.120
Don't be tellin' people's fortunes without their permission.

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:02.540
"You and the girl of your heart are rapidly approaching!"

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:06.800
It must be talking about me and Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:12.970
"An 'A' is in your future"

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:14.140
"A"?!

00:07:14.140 --> 00:07:17.060
Oh, geez. How old of a game is that thing?

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:19.560
Hey. What does "A" mean?

00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:24.400
The letter A, you see, is the one before the letter B...

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:27.400
So it means fried shrimp!
<i>("AB" sounds like "ebi" which is shrimp)</i>

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.030
Oh. So it doesn't mean "kiss".
<i>(It actually does mean "kiss")</i>

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:38.500
Sorry! Sorry! I overslept!...Huh?

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.670
--Geez! What took you so long, Doc?!
--Geez! What took you so long, Doc?!
--Geez! What took you so long, Doc?!

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.460
Sorry...

00:07:50.170 --> 00:07:51.630
Awesome!

00:07:51.630 --> 00:07:53.800
Look at all the planes!

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:04.020
I hear you can even play a helicopter flight simulator here!

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:06.060
--That sounds like fun!
--Yeah!

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:07.860
Too bad!

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:09.360
Why's that, Conan?

00:08:09.360 --> 00:08:14.200
It says here only fifth graders and up can do the flight simulator!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.410
Aww, that's no fun.

00:08:16.410 --> 00:08:20.910
Sorry, I played it to death when I got into 5th grade.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:27.460
In that case, how about I tell you all an interesting story?

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:31.050
Hey. We're in for a long story if we don't stop him now.

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.550
Leave it to me.

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.890
The "Pegasus" from Greek mythology is-

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:37.640
Tadah! And now for a quiz!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.390
Huh? What're you doing?

00:08:40.390 --> 00:08:43.810
Three people who were born on New Year's Day, April Fool's Day,

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.270
and Children's Day all got together and formed a club!

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.150
So, what was their club's name?

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:53.570
Here's a hint: it's a flying animal, much like the Pegasus!

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:55.950
A flying animal?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.910
Oh? You figured it out, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:09:00.910 --> 00:09:04.540
Of course! You just need to add their birthdays, right?

00:09:04.540 --> 00:09:06.250
--Eh?
--Birthdays?

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:11.760
January 1st, April 1st,
May 5th... October 7th?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:15.010
Yep! October 7th!

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:19.560
It's the <i>Tonakai</i> (Reindeer)!
<i>(to = 10, na =7, kai = club)</i>

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:23.560
And they fly while pulling a sled on Christmas, right?

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:27.270
Correct! You're so smart, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:33.400
Hey! Isn't that Shishido Eimei?!

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.080
--So cool!
--So cool!

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.700
"Mori Detective Agency"

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.800
--Thank you!
--Next, please!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.180
"To Mori Ran"

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:03.680
Alright! Here you go!

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:07.190
Thank you so much! I'm a big fan of yours, Nishina-<i>san</i>!

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:10.520
Please continue to write lots of delicious books!

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.650
That's a unique comment. Thank you.

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:19.160
He's even hotter than he is in pictures!

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:21.740
His type is my favorite!

00:10:21.740 --> 00:10:23.330
You're so silly, Sonoko...

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:31.960
--What a reckless driver!
--Isn't that...

00:10:42.010 --> 00:10:44.640
It is Osanai Nana, the model!

00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:47.100
I have no interest in women.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.560
Let's get some tea!

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:55.150
What time do you have dinner with your mom?

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:56.280
7:00.

00:10:56.280 --> 00:10:58.820
Did you set it up again this time too?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:10:59.700
Yeah.

00:10:59.700 --> 00:11:02.070
You sure have it rough, too.

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:05.660
What was it, ten years ago when your mom left?

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.540
Yeah. When I was seven...

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:12.040
...I remember them having a big argument.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.420
Apparently they split because of personality conflicts.

00:11:15.420 --> 00:11:17.670
And then in no time flat...

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:23.300
...your mom began to flourish as a lawyer, right?

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.850
In contrast, your dad quit his job as a police detective,

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.190
and became a lousy private eye instead.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:33.980
Wha?

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:40.400
Yeah! Your dad's suddenly all famous and stuff now,

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:44.490
but I bet he would've ruined himself by now had you not been there.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:53.880
I don't think so, but my mom was really with-it in that regard.

00:11:53.880 --> 00:11:55.790
I'm back!

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:57.300
Welcome back!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.420
Huh? He's still not ready?

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:05.220
He went to play mahjong during lunch and just got back now!

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:09.890
Geez! Why do I hafta eat dinner with Eri?!

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:14.650
Please quit complaining and get ready already.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:18.940
<i>I'm here at the house of Asahi Katsuyoshi-<i>san,</i></i>

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:20.610
<i>owner of Aqua Crystal,</i>

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:26.070
<i>the aquatic recreation center opening today by the Touto Bay!</i>

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:29.950
Conan-<i>kun.</i>

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:31.620
I'll change too!

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:42.510
Sorry, Mom! We ran a little late!

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:48.310
That's all right. I'm sure "someone" was busy playing mahjong.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:52.520
She's as sharp as ever.

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:56.060
I gotta watch what I say around this lady...

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:58.320
Hello, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.610
H-hello!

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:03.070
You're so scatterbrained, Tsuji-<i>san</i>!

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.860
Oh! Long time, no see, Mori-<i>san</i>!

00:13:05.860 --> 00:13:07.870
Oh! Tsuji-<i>san</i>!

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.330
Who's Mori?

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:11.450
You know, the detective.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:14.540
--The famous detective?!
--Mori Kogoro?!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:18.420
Yes. I am detective Mori Kogoro.

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:21.840
Oh, Tsuji-<i>san</i>! Let me introduce my family!

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:24.670
This is my wife Eri, and my daughter Ran.

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:26.640
And that's Conan, the mooch.

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:30.180
Isn't there any other way to say that?!

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:33.850
I'm Tsuji. I played with Mori-<i>san</i> in a pro-amateur golf tournament.

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:35.350
That reminds me, Tsuji-<i>san.</i>

00:13:35.350 --> 00:13:39.110
Doesn't the All-American Open begin next Thursday?

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:44.110
Yes! I basically practiced an entire year for this one tournament!

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:47.660
This year, I will make it to the top ten for sure!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:48.870
I look forward to it!

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:52.370
But sometimes it's important to take a breather,

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:56.040
so I thought I might take the girls out for a flight tomorrow.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:14:01.500
Tsuji-<i>san</i> here also owns and pilots his own helicopter, you see.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.550
Say! I'm planning to fly the following Thursday, too!

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.880
Why don't you come along?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.890
Wow! Really?!

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.050
Sounds wonderful!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:12.140
Yay!

00:14:12.140 --> 00:14:17.560
No, uhh, flying isn't really my thing, so maybe some other time.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.730
Oh? That's too bad.

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.400
He's no fun.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:29.360
That man's name is Sawaki-<i>san,</i>

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.080
and he's known my mom and dad since they were young.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.710
What's that grape badge for?

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:44.960
That's the symbol of a sommelier.

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:50.760
Oh, a sommelier is someone like
Sawaki-<i>san</i> who specializes in wine.

00:14:52.350 --> 00:14:54.260
What's that around his neck?

00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:58.850
That's a "tastevin".
It's for taste-testing wine!

00:14:58.850 --> 00:15:01.400
Whoa, you really know your stuff.

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:03.610
I read about it in Nishida-<i>san</i>'s books!

00:15:03.610 --> 00:15:06.400
For example, red wine is best at room temperature,

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:09.070
and white wine and rose are best chilled!

00:15:09.070 --> 00:15:11.740
It's true that many people say that,

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:15.410
but a wine's best temperature is really up to personal preference.

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:26.000
Excellent.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.800
Light red wine is actually quite delicious when chilled.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:34.600
The key is that a wine's astringency is diminished when cooled.

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:35.760
Really?

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:38.140
Still, I can't believe you're old enough

00:15:38.140 --> 00:15:41.140
to be interested in that sort of thing now.

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:45.820
That just means that we've gotten that much older.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.280
That's for sure.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:53.820
They seem to be getting along well now!

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.470
Oh, Conan-<i>kun</i>! Your mouth's all messy!

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:14.090
N-no, that's okay...

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.350
Come on, now! Don't move!

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.600
"An 'A' is in your future"

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:19.600
An "A" is in your future?

00:16:22.690 --> 00:16:25.810
Sheesh! Kids are such a pain!

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.230
Urgh!

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.900
That was delicious.

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:37.240
The wine and food here tastes just like it did back then!

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:40.330
Say. Do you remember?

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:44.040
When we first came to this restaurant 15 years ago,

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:46.250
you gave me a present.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:50.420
Yeah. Your favorite Zigoba chocolates.

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:54.180
And then we ate them all on a bench at Beika Park on our way home.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.220
Oh, that's right.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.150
Towako-<i>san</i>!

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:10.730
Who's he?!

00:17:10.730 --> 00:17:12.400
Isn't that Peter Ford?

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.610
You know. He often hosts TV shows and stuff.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:19.280
Dammit! What's she doing with him?!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:22.580
Who's Towako-<i>san</i>?

00:17:22.580 --> 00:17:24.790
She runs a hostess club in Ginza.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.920
She's been extra generous whenever I've-

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:31.590
I should be going now.

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:35.680
Already? I thought we might have some coffee back-

00:17:35.680 --> 00:17:38.260
I'm sorry. I still have work to finish.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.680
Thank you for the meal.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:44.140
Mom!

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:46.770
Dad!

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:51.820
Towako-<i>san</i> disappeared somewhere!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.900
The old guy never learns...

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:17.970
Come on in.

00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:20.390
"Megure Juzo" "Megure Jusan"?

00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:23.310
It's read "Juzo".

00:18:23.310 --> 00:18:25.140
Oh!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.890
Oh, Genta-<i>kun</i>!

00:18:27.890 --> 00:18:30.360
So Inspector Megure's name is Juzo, huh?

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:35.280
Oh, Mori-<i>kun</i>! You came all this way?
And everyone else, too?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:40.240
We were all just about to go hiking.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:42.490
Inspector. How is your injury?

00:18:42.490 --> 00:18:47.460
Luckily, it missed a vital spot, so there's no danger to his life,

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:50.170
but they say he'll need to stay here for a few days.

00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:52.500
Hey, Inspector.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.340
Why do you always have a hat on?

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:58.010
Oh, uh, does it really matter?

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:02.100
--I bet he's barely got hair!
--He could have huge bumps!

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:06.020
We believe a handgun-type crossbow was used.

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.020
We're investigating this from two directions:

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:15.230
whether he was attacked specifically, or just for fun as he passed by.

00:19:15.230 --> 00:19:19.030
Hey, old inspector guy!
Didn't you have a gun?!

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:21.360
And you still let him get away?

00:19:21.360 --> 00:19:24.530
Of course he wouldn't have a gun on him while jogging!

00:19:24.530 --> 00:19:31.620
Plus, even if I had had one, I'm a horrible shot, unlike Mori-<i>kun</i> here.

00:19:31.620 --> 00:19:34.880
Eh?! My dad is good with guns?!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:39.170
Enough to have been one of the best shots on the entire force!

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:42.430
I guess everyone's good at something...

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:48.560
However, something odd was found where the crossbow was fired.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.100
Here it is.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:53.270
--What is it?
--It looks like a Western sword.

00:19:53.270 --> 00:19:56.900
Huh?! I've seen this somewhere before!

00:19:56.900 --> 00:19:58.360
But where?

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:08.910
--Good morning!
--Good morning!

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:11.160
That's a pretty broach.

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:32.270
Here is your schedule for today, <i>Sensei.</i>

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.360
And I found this in the mailbox downstairs.

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:37.900
Oh, Zigoba!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:41.490
Those are your favorite
Swiss chocolates, aren't they?

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:44.280
Ah! So he...

00:20:44.280 --> 00:20:48.410
But I don't see the sender's name...

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:51.370
It's all right. I know who's responsible for it.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:55.120
Wow!

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:06.180
Water! Water...

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.560
Sensei!

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.150
How's my mother?!

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:20.610
Rest easy!

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:25.150
We flushed her stomach immediately, so there's no danger to her life!

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:27.370
Thank goodness...

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.030
Was it poison, then?

00:21:29.030 --> 00:21:32.700
Yes. We believe it was agrochemical in type.

00:21:35.790 --> 00:21:37.960
Mom!

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.090
Mom...

00:21:39.090 --> 00:21:40.300
Ran...

00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:41.750
Eri...

00:21:41.750 --> 00:21:44.510
You're here too, dear?

00:21:44.510 --> 00:21:46.760
Are you okay, lady?

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:48.220
Even you, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:50.680
Thank you. I'm okay now.

00:21:50.680 --> 00:21:55.640
Just to be safe, she should probably stay here for today.

00:21:55.640 --> 00:21:57.650
Sounds good to me.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:04.440
Still, first the inspector, and now Eri...
Is this just coincidence?

00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:07.910
Incidentally, I hear she collapsed the moment she ate some chocolate?

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.660
Yes. It was apparently in the agency's mailbox.

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:13.200
Zigoba!

00:22:13.200 --> 00:22:16.330
A-and... this paper flower!

00:22:16.330 --> 00:22:19.380
You don't mean... the same person did this?!

00:22:19.380 --> 00:22:21.710
Huh? That flower...

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:24.630
Where?! Where have I seen it?!

00:22:24.630 --> 00:22:29.680
But why would someone so cautious eat poisoned chocolate?

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:35.520
Yeah. The old man got Ran's mom mad at dinner the other night.

00:22:35.520 --> 00:22:38.480
Apparently she mistook it as his apology.

00:22:38.480 --> 00:22:40.100
Ah.

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:42.520
Here you are! Repairs complete!

00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:50.200
Who pulled this prank?!

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:53.160
Doc! Don't open it!

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:01.250
Doc!

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:06.010
I'm fine! Go after him, Shinichi!

00:23:06.010 --> 00:23:06.960
But!

00:23:08.470 --> 00:23:10.300
Go, Shinichi! Go after him!

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:11.390
Got it!

00:23:28.820 --> 00:23:30.780
Which way did he go?!

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:34.410
Ayumi and Genta live down this left street...

00:23:34.410 --> 00:23:35.660
Alright!

00:23:40.120 --> 00:23:42.000
Oh, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.090
A black off-road motorcycle?

00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:47.380
What's a black pot-holed motorcycle?

00:23:50.510 --> 00:23:54.510
That's it! That's the off-road motorcycle, Genta-<i>Kun</i>!

00:23:54.510 --> 00:23:55.720
C-Conan!

00:23:55.720 --> 00:23:56.760
Roger that!

00:23:56.760 --> 00:23:58.270
So he did turn left!

00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:05.820
Conan-<i>kun</i>! He just turned right, toward Beika Station!

00:24:05.820 --> 00:24:06.770
Roger that!

00:24:06.770 --> 00:24:08.530
Alright! I gotta beat him there!

00:24:17.160 --> 00:24:19.160
Yes! Found ya!

00:24:29.670 --> 00:24:32.300
Oh, no, you don't! I'm not letting you get away!

00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:39.680
Are you okay, lady?!

00:24:39.680 --> 00:24:41.560
Thank you!

00:24:53.200 --> 00:24:55.360
What's this?

00:24:55.360 --> 00:24:58.240
That's it! I figured it out!

00:24:59.290 --> 00:25:00.660
Playing cards?

00:25:00.660 --> 00:25:01.370
Yeah.

00:25:01.370 --> 00:25:05.460
The culprit is doing these crimes to match the pictures on the cards.

00:25:05.460 --> 00:25:09.710
Inspector Megure was attacked first, and his name is Juzo, right?

00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:13.050
It's written as "thirteen", thus the King of Spades!

00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:17.180
Doesn't this king's sword look like the one found at the scene?

00:25:20.010 --> 00:25:25.140
Next, Ran's mother's name, Kisaki, means "Queen" in English.

00:25:25.140 --> 00:25:27.480
Hence the Queen of Spades.

00:25:27.480 --> 00:25:32.570
This queen's flower is the same one that was on the chocolate box!

00:25:34.150 --> 00:25:36.110
He's right! They're the same!

00:25:36.110 --> 00:25:39.240
But how are Dr. Agasa and "eleven" related?

00:25:39.240 --> 00:25:41.700
The doc's name is Agasa Hiroshi,

00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:44.750
and the "shi" in his name is a combination of 10 and 1!

00:25:44.750 --> 00:25:47.080
Hence the Jack of Spades.

00:25:47.080 --> 00:25:51.380
"Jack" originally refers to soldiers, thus this sword-like object...

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:55.880
They're the same! No doubt about it!

00:25:55.880 --> 00:26:00.260
But why playing cards? And why spades?

00:26:00.260 --> 00:26:03.060
Spades refer to death.

00:26:03.060 --> 00:26:05.600
Similarly, hearts refer to love,

00:26:05.600 --> 00:26:09.560
diamonds refer to money, and clubs refer to happiness.

00:26:09.560 --> 00:26:14.070
Then is the culprit planning to follow the playing cards in order

00:26:14.070 --> 00:26:18.200
and kill people with the numbers 13 to 1 in their names?

00:26:18.200 --> 00:26:21.160
More specifically, people connected to you.

00:26:25.580 --> 00:26:27.710
But who would do this?

00:26:27.710 --> 00:26:30.590
Our only clue was the motorcycle's license plate number,

00:26:30.590 --> 00:26:32.210
but it turned out to be stolen.

00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:35.590
Inspector!

00:26:35.590 --> 00:26:37.300
What are you doing here?

00:26:37.300 --> 00:26:41.600
I heard that first Eri-<i>san</i> was attacked, then Dr. Agasa too...

00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:44.100
But what about your wound?

00:26:44.100 --> 00:26:47.520
It's been sewed up! I'm fine!

00:26:47.520 --> 00:26:51.560
I heard everything. The culprit is most likely Murakami Joe.

00:26:51.560 --> 00:26:53.770
Murakami Joe?!

00:26:53.770 --> 00:26:55.480
Who is he?

00:26:55.480 --> 00:26:59.280
A maverick gambling dealer.

00:26:59.280 --> 00:27:02.030
He committed a murder ten years ago,

00:27:02.030 --> 00:27:05.870
and was just released one week ago on parole.

00:27:05.870 --> 00:27:08.040
A gambling dealer?

00:27:08.040 --> 00:27:11.790
A person who deals out cards to gambling patrons.

00:27:11.790 --> 00:27:14.500
This is Murakami Joe, 10 years ago.

00:27:16.960 --> 00:27:18.510
Murakami, huh...

00:27:18.510 --> 00:27:22.470
It's true that I wouldn't be surprised if he held a grudge against me.

00:27:22.470 --> 00:27:23.720
Why's that?

00:27:23.720 --> 00:27:25.970
Because I arrested him.

00:27:25.970 --> 00:27:30.230
Hold on! It's only natural that policemen arrest criminals!

00:27:30.230 --> 00:27:32.190
That's true, but...

00:27:32.190 --> 00:27:35.400
Actually, I have heard about that incident.

00:27:35.400 --> 00:27:38.490
If I'm not mistaken, after he was taken to the police station...

00:27:38.490 --> 00:27:42.870
Shiratori-<i>Kun</i>! We don't need to hear the story!

00:27:42.870 --> 00:27:47.370
But why wouldn't Murakami Joe come straight after me?

00:27:47.370 --> 00:27:49.830
He could deal with me directly...

00:27:49.830 --> 00:27:55.420
Probably to make you suffer.
So as to ruin you slowly but surely.

00:27:57.670 --> 00:28:02.890
Say, is there anyone you know with a "ten" in their name?!

00:28:02.890 --> 00:28:06.390
They might be the next person to be attacked!

00:28:06.390 --> 00:28:10.310
Ten... <i>"Juu"..."To"...</i>

00:28:10.310 --> 00:28:11.850
Towako-<i>san</i>!

00:28:29.410 --> 00:28:31.960
--Welcome.
--Welcome.

00:28:31.960 --> 00:28:34.250
Oh! Mori-<i>sensei</i>!

00:28:34.250 --> 00:28:35.670
Towako-<i>san</i>!

00:28:35.670 --> 00:28:37.840
You're all right!

00:28:37.840 --> 00:28:41.220
"All right?" Did something happen?

00:28:44.470 --> 00:28:49.060
Umm, Shiratori-<i>san</i>. What were you going to say back at the hospital?

00:28:49.060 --> 00:28:51.770
You know, about that Murakami guy!

00:28:51.770 --> 00:28:56.270
Oh. Well, I guess I'll tell you since you could find out easily enough.

00:28:56.270 --> 00:28:59.780
I heard this from a superior officer.

00:28:59.780 --> 00:29:02.990
Ten years ago, when Mori-<i>san</i> was a police detective,

00:29:02.990 --> 00:29:04.740
he and Inspector Megure-

00:29:04.740 --> 00:29:07.990
Or was he still an assistant inspector back then?

00:29:07.990 --> 00:29:12.410
In any case, the two of them arrested Murakami Joe for murder.

00:29:16.790 --> 00:29:20.130
While they were interrogating him at the police station,

00:29:20.130 --> 00:29:23.300
Murakami said he wanted to use the restroom.

00:29:23.300 --> 00:29:28.970
Mori-<i>san</i> and the inspector ordered an officer to take him there,

00:29:28.970 --> 00:29:31.810
then took a smoke break in front of the interrogation room.

00:29:31.810 --> 00:29:37.100
Just then, you and your mother arrived to bring a change of clothes.

00:29:38.900 --> 00:29:41.320
That's when it happened.

00:29:42.900 --> 00:29:48.570
Murakami managed to steal the officer's gun in the restroom.

00:29:48.570 --> 00:29:50.740
I remember.

00:29:50.740 --> 00:29:52.910
Just then, I...

00:30:04.090 --> 00:30:05.880
Get a car ready!

00:30:05.880 --> 00:30:09.140
This woman and I have a rendezvous at the ends of Hell!

00:30:10.720 --> 00:30:11.640
Mom!

00:30:11.640 --> 00:30:13.640
Ran! Stay away!

00:30:34.830 --> 00:30:37.040
Mori-<i>kun.</i>

00:30:37.040 --> 00:30:40.170
What's on your mind?

00:30:40.170 --> 00:30:42.040
Oh, nothing!

00:30:46.050 --> 00:30:50.300
You're saying he shot her?!

00:30:50.300 --> 00:30:53.470
I had forgotten until just now!

00:30:53.470 --> 00:30:57.430
It must've been something you didn't want to remember.

00:30:57.430 --> 00:31:01.310
But... But why would Dad shoot her?!

00:31:01.310 --> 00:31:04.530
He must've been really confident about his skill.

00:31:04.530 --> 00:31:08.200
Confident he could miss the hostage and hit only the criminal...

00:31:08.200 --> 00:31:11.450
But the bullet missed and hit your mother instead.

00:31:14.870 --> 00:31:17.660
Apparently, the fact he shot without concern for the hostage

00:31:17.660 --> 00:31:21.080
caused quite some trouble for him at the police station, too...

00:31:21.080 --> 00:31:25.340
I believe it was soon afterward that your father left the force.

00:31:39.850 --> 00:31:40.390
Hello?

00:31:40.390 --> 00:31:42.230
Hey, Ran! Been a while!

00:31:42.230 --> 00:31:43.770
Shinichi?!

00:31:43.770 --> 00:31:46.110
Dr. Agasa filled me in on everything.

00:31:46.110 --> 00:31:48.780
Sounds like some bad stuff is going down.

00:31:48.780 --> 00:31:53.660
It's much more than "bad"!
Where are you?! Come back right away!

00:31:53.660 --> 00:31:59.460
Sorry, I'm in the middle of a case here.
I won't be back for a while.

00:31:59.460 --> 00:32:00.580
Oh...

00:32:00.580 --> 00:32:03.130
Don't get all glum on me!

00:32:03.130 --> 00:32:06.670
But the doc and the inspector gave me a summary of what's up,

00:32:06.670 --> 00:32:09.340
so if I figure anything out,
I'll call right away!

00:32:09.340 --> 00:32:13.720
Tell me. Would you shoot, Shinichi?

00:32:13.720 --> 00:32:18.970
I found out why my mom really left my dad.

00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:24.980
The Kogoro-<i>san</i> shot your mom, huh...

00:32:24.980 --> 00:32:30.820
I don't care how confident he was...
I can't believe what he did.

00:32:30.820 --> 00:32:34.490
You would never do anything like that, right, Shinichi?!

00:32:34.490 --> 00:32:38.450
Good question... I dunno.

00:32:38.450 --> 00:32:42.210
But even if it's a fact that your dad shot your mom,

00:32:42.210 --> 00:32:46.170
are you sure that equals the truth behind it?

00:32:46.170 --> 00:32:48.840
What do you mean?!
That doesn't make sense!

00:32:48.840 --> 00:32:51.760
Anyways, that's all I can say.

00:32:51.760 --> 00:32:53.340
Cheer up, Ran!

00:32:53.340 --> 00:32:54.680
Later!

00:32:54.680 --> 00:32:56.140
Wait!

00:32:56.140 --> 00:32:59.180
Shinichi?! Shinichi?!

00:33:07.520 --> 00:33:09.480
The truth...

00:33:23.870 --> 00:33:26.580
Inspector! I'll watch the emergency exit!

00:33:26.580 --> 00:33:28.750
Wait! Mori-<i>kun</i>!

00:33:32.260 --> 00:33:35.380
He gets really fired up when there's a pretty woman involved...

00:33:50.230 --> 00:33:53.490
The old guy never came home...

00:33:56.030 --> 00:34:03.410
Still, why would Murakami Joe leave clues that point straight to him?

00:34:04.660 --> 00:34:08.420
Is he trying to challenge the old guy and the police?

00:34:08.420 --> 00:34:14.340
But how did Murakami research his acquaintances from behind bars?

00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:18.220
He even knew Ran's mother's favorite brand of chocolate...

00:34:22.260 --> 00:34:25.350
"Tsuji Hiroki"

00:34:25.890 --> 00:34:27.940
Tsuji Hiroki...

00:34:27.940 --> 00:34:29.440
Tsuji...

00:34:28.190 --> 00:34:30.310
"Ten"

00:34:30.650 --> 00:34:33.480
Tsuji Hiroki? The pro golfer?

00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:38.320
Yes! Conan-<i>kun</i> noticed it, but Tsuji's name has a "ten" in it!

00:34:38.320 --> 00:34:39.700
Tsuji...

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:41.830
She's right! There is one!

00:34:41.830 --> 00:34:46.960
I called his home, but he left for the heliport 30 minutes ago!

00:34:46.960 --> 00:34:48.040
Got it!

00:34:48.040 --> 00:34:52.210
Contact the station and have them send someone to keep watch here.

00:34:52.210 --> 00:34:53.300
Yes, sir!

00:34:58.010 --> 00:35:00.090
Conan-<i>kun</i>! Let's go, too!

00:35:04.640 --> 00:35:06.930
Let's go, Mori-<i>kun</i>!

00:35:06.930 --> 00:35:09.480
Go? To get breakfast?

00:35:23.740 --> 00:35:25.240
Dad!

00:35:26.580 --> 00:35:29.290
Hey, you! What're you doing here?!

00:35:29.290 --> 00:35:33.380
Don't give us that!
We're involved in this too, you know!

00:35:33.380 --> 00:35:35.500
I'm your daughter!

00:35:37.170 --> 00:35:41.840
So, people connected to Mori-<i>san</i> are being attacked one by one?

00:35:41.840 --> 00:35:44.930
Yes. Counting down from 13.

00:35:44.930 --> 00:35:48.480
And since you're #10, you're in danger now!

00:35:48.480 --> 00:35:51.520
Anyways, it'd be wise to cancel your flight for today.

00:35:51.520 --> 00:35:52.980
I'll be fine!

00:35:52.980 --> 00:35:57.690
If you're that worried, why don't you and Mori-<i>san</i> come with me?

00:35:57.690 --> 00:35:59.860
No, flying isn't really-

00:35:59.860 --> 00:36:02.530
Incidentally, where is your flight to today?

00:36:02.530 --> 00:36:06.370
Touto Airport. With other places along the way, though.

00:36:06.370 --> 00:36:09.000
When did you submit your flight plan?

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:12.830
Hmm... The day before yesterday, at the Aviation Bureau.

00:36:12.830 --> 00:36:13.750
Inspector.

00:36:13.750 --> 00:36:17.710
There's a chance Murakami is lying in wait at Touto Airport.

00:36:17.710 --> 00:36:21.130
Alright! You head for
Touto Airport in the car!

00:36:21.130 --> 00:36:22.430
Yes, sir!

00:36:22.430 --> 00:36:27.310
Mori-<i>Kun</i>! Just to be safe, we're going to ride the helicopter, too!

00:36:27.310 --> 00:36:30.680
Ran-<i>kun</i>! I know how you feel, but this is as far as you go.

00:36:30.680 --> 00:36:32.810
But!

00:36:32.810 --> 00:36:35.110
Fine.

00:36:35.110 --> 00:36:38.690
Inspector! I'd prefer to go with Detective Shiratori in the car!

00:36:38.690 --> 00:36:40.570
Are you trying to run away on your own?!

00:36:40.570 --> 00:36:42.570
I, uhh, need to use the restroom!

00:36:51.160 --> 00:36:53.710
I-Inspector! I don't want to die too!

00:36:53.710 --> 00:36:56.080
Get in! If you die, we'll die together!

00:36:56.080 --> 00:36:58.090
So we are gonna die!

00:37:12.730 --> 00:37:14.350
Well, I'm off.

00:37:16.690 --> 00:37:19.900
Conan-<i>kun</i>. We should get going-

00:37:19.900 --> 00:37:21.940
Huh? Where are you?!

00:37:23.240 --> 00:37:24.530
He couldn't be!

00:37:28.780 --> 00:37:31.290
One sheep! Two sheep!

00:37:31.290 --> 00:37:33.540
Is that an anti-crashing spell?

00:37:33.540 --> 00:37:36.210
-Conan-<i>kun</i>!
--When did you get in here?!

00:37:36.210 --> 00:37:41.130
I always wanted to try sitting next to a pilot's seat!

00:37:41.130 --> 00:37:43.420
Welcome to my cockpit!

00:37:43.420 --> 00:37:46.470
We're scheduled to fly over your place on Beika Street, you know!

00:37:46.470 --> 00:37:48.470
Yay! That's great!

00:37:48.470 --> 00:37:51.520
We have no choice.
We can't exactly go back now.

00:37:51.520 --> 00:37:54.430
But if you cause any trouble,
I'm tossin' you out!

00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:13.120
Nothing seems out of the ordinary...

00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:14.370
Whatcha lookin' at?

00:38:14.370 --> 00:38:17.830
You're in a helicopter here!
Take a look outside!

00:38:20.920 --> 00:38:22.090
Is something the matter?

00:38:22.090 --> 00:38:23.590
Not at all.

00:38:23.590 --> 00:38:27.930
Say, you applied some eyedrops earlier.
Do you always use them?

00:38:27.930 --> 00:38:33.850
Yeah, when I'm driving, or when
I'm piloting my helicopter.

00:38:33.850 --> 00:38:35.890
Beika Street's coming up now!

00:38:35.890 --> 00:38:37.350
So it is!

00:38:40.400 --> 00:38:42.730
Mori-<i>Kun</i>! There's your place, too!

00:38:42.730 --> 00:38:44.480
I don't wanna look!

00:38:55.700 --> 00:38:56.540
What's wrong?!

00:38:56.540 --> 00:38:58.330
It's too bright! I can't open my eyes!

00:38:58.330 --> 00:38:59.620
Say what?!

00:38:59.620 --> 00:39:01.670
Wait! Were those eyedrops-!

00:39:01.670 --> 00:39:03.460
--Does that mean...
--Does that mean...

00:39:06.340 --> 00:39:08.760
Mister! We're drifting to the left!

00:39:12.140 --> 00:39:15.270
M-Mori-<i>kun</i>! Do you know how to fly?!

00:39:15.270 --> 00:39:17.100
Of course I don't!

00:39:17.100 --> 00:39:19.310
We can't stay in the air like this!

00:39:19.310 --> 00:39:22.730
I gotta find a place we can land!

00:39:22.730 --> 00:39:25.110
Teitan Elementary! Alright!

00:39:25.110 --> 00:39:26.280
Huh?!

00:39:26.280 --> 00:39:27.780
I'm gonna land us in the schoolyard!

00:39:27.780 --> 00:39:30.240
You handle the pedals and corrective measures!

00:39:30.240 --> 00:39:34.030
Wha?! You idiot! No! Stop!
Are you trying to kill us?!

00:39:34.030 --> 00:39:38.120
Don't worry! I did lots of flight simulator practice when I was a kid!

00:39:38.120 --> 00:39:40.580
B-but you still are a kid...

00:39:40.580 --> 00:39:43.250
Tsuji-<i>san</i>! We're gonna crash if we don't do something now!

00:39:43.250 --> 00:39:44.540
Help me out!

00:39:46.710 --> 00:39:48.840
Alright! Let's do it!

00:39:48.840 --> 00:39:50.680
A-are you serious?!

00:39:50.680 --> 00:39:54.300
Elevation, 300 feet!
Speed, 40 knots! Go ahead!

00:39:54.300 --> 00:39:56.180
H-here goes!

00:40:01.940 --> 00:40:04.940
Elevation, 200 feet! Speed, 30 knots!

00:40:04.940 --> 00:40:06.570
Press the right pedal 10 degrees!

00:40:09.570 --> 00:40:12.570
The schoolyard is dead-ahead!
Distance, 500 feet!

00:40:14.240 --> 00:40:16.450
Hey, Genta! Do you read me?! Genta!

00:40:16.450 --> 00:40:17.580
Conan?!

00:40:17.580 --> 00:40:21.370
I'm about to emergency land a helicopter!
Get everyone out of there!

00:40:21.370 --> 00:40:23.130
Helicopter?

00:40:25.130 --> 00:40:30.050
Everyone! Run! A helicopter's about to crash!

00:40:30.050 --> 00:40:31.550
Like hell it's gonna crash!

00:40:33.800 --> 00:40:37.640
We're spinning left!
Hit the right pedal hard!

00:40:37.640 --> 00:40:40.020
Oh no! We're in a downwash!

00:40:49.820 --> 00:40:51.240
It really did crash!

00:40:51.240 --> 00:40:53.610
Is Conan-<i>kun</i> in there?!

00:40:55.740 --> 00:40:57.700
I'm alive!

00:40:58.910 --> 00:41:00.370
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:41:00.370 --> 00:41:02.160
Are you all right, Tsuji-<i>san</i>?!

00:41:05.420 --> 00:41:06.500
The fuel is leaking!

00:41:06.500 --> 00:41:07.840
--What?!
--What?!

00:41:19.310 --> 00:41:20.770
It exploded!

00:41:20.770 --> 00:41:23.230
Aren't helicopters expensive?!

00:41:23.230 --> 00:41:26.860
Don't just the rotors alone cost 10 million yen?

00:41:26.860 --> 00:41:28.980
How many boxed eel lunches is that?

00:41:35.740 --> 00:41:38.410
I'm glad everyone is all right.

00:41:38.280 --> 00:41:39.950
"Agasa Hiroshi"

00:41:38.410 --> 00:41:42.120
But, Doc! Conan's unfair!

00:41:42.120 --> 00:41:45.460
He got to pilot a real helicopter all by himself...

00:41:45.460 --> 00:41:48.500
That's not the issue here!
We just about died, you know!

00:41:48.500 --> 00:41:50.130
About that...

00:41:50.130 --> 00:41:55.380
Tsuji-<i>san</i>'s vitamin eyedrops had been switched with dilation drops.

00:41:55.380 --> 00:41:57.140
Dilation drops?

00:41:57.140 --> 00:42:03.140
Medicine used to open up the pupils to treat pseudomyopia and such.

00:42:03.140 --> 00:42:06.900
Ah. So that's why the sunlight overwhelmed his eyes...

00:42:06.900 --> 00:42:11.610
Except the ones Tsuji-<i>san</i> used are to treat something called "iritis".

00:42:11.610 --> 00:42:13.690
Iritis?

00:42:13.690 --> 00:42:15.650
How are they different?

00:42:17.200 --> 00:42:22.240
Pseudomyopia drops take effect in 5 minutes, and don't last long.

00:42:22.240 --> 00:42:28.460
Conversely, iritis drops take a half hour to work, and last a long time.

00:42:28.460 --> 00:42:30.250
A long time?

00:42:30.250 --> 00:42:35.090
It varies per person, but they usually dilate the eyes for 10 to 14 days.

00:42:35.090 --> 00:42:36.260
That long?!

00:42:36.260 --> 00:42:40.050
Then what about Thursday's
All-American Open?!

00:42:40.050 --> 00:42:44.680
He probably has no choice but to cancel...

00:42:44.680 --> 00:42:48.100
Say, when did the culprit switch the eyedrops?

00:42:48.100 --> 00:42:50.150
About that...

00:42:50.150 --> 00:42:53.480
This morning, after Tsuji-<i>san</i> took his car out of the garage,

00:42:53.480 --> 00:42:56.860
he apparently applied his eyedrops in the car.

00:42:56.860 --> 00:43:01.070
Immediately after, he heard glass break,

00:43:01.070 --> 00:43:06.710
so he left the eyedrops on the center console and went back inside.

00:43:06.710 --> 00:43:10.750
Apparently, a rock had been thrown through a window.

00:43:10.750 --> 00:43:11.880
A rock?

00:43:11.880 --> 00:43:14.340
That's what happened to Dr. Agasa!

00:43:14.340 --> 00:43:17.800
However, Tsuji-<i>san</i> figured it was just some kid's prank,

00:43:17.800 --> 00:43:21.340
so he had the maids take care of it and left.

00:43:21.340 --> 00:43:24.640
There's no question that the culprit threw the rock!

00:43:24.640 --> 00:43:29.270
And Tsuji-<i>san</i>'s eyedrops were switched while he was in the house!

00:43:29.270 --> 00:43:31.860
Yes. Most likely.

00:43:31.860 --> 00:43:33.060
Inspector.

00:43:34.980 --> 00:43:37.820
There is no doubt that
Murakami Joe is responsible.

00:43:37.820 --> 00:43:39.990
We found this.

00:43:39.990 --> 00:43:42.320
The 10 of Spades...

00:43:43.410 --> 00:43:46.750
Mori-<i>Kun</i>! "Nine" is the next one to be attacked!

00:43:46.750 --> 00:43:50.040
Do you know anyone with a "nine" in their name?!

00:43:50.040 --> 00:43:54.500
--I can't think of anyone.
I do know an "eight" though.
--Eight?

00:43:54.500 --> 00:43:56.670
Sawaki-<i>san</i>, a sommelier.

00:43:55.170 --> 00:43:59.300
"Sawaki Kohei"

00:43:56.670 --> 00:44:01.760
His name is Kohei-<i>san</i>, and the upper part of his "ko" is "eight"!

00:43:59.300 --> 00:44:01.760
"Ko"

00:44:01.760 --> 00:44:05.010
Alright! Let's meet this Sawaki fellow!

00:44:08.060 --> 00:44:12.810
So this Murakami person is attacking your acquaintances one by one

00:44:12.810 --> 00:44:15.690
to get revenge on you, Mori-<i>san</i>?

00:44:15.690 --> 00:44:16.820
Yes.

00:44:16.820 --> 00:44:20.820
Still, you certainly do seem calm, Mori-<i>san...</i>

00:44:20.820 --> 00:44:26.240
Oh, I'm "five", so I still have lots of time until I get attacked!

00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:30.830
Wine...

00:44:30.830 --> 00:44:35.920
That's called a "wine cooler".
It keeps wine at the proper temperature.

00:44:35.920 --> 00:44:38.510
There sure is a lot in it!

00:44:38.510 --> 00:44:41.880
Sawaki-<i>san</i>'s family has an orchard in Yamanashi,

00:44:41.880 --> 00:44:45.930
and he has hundreds of bottles of wine stored there!

00:44:45.930 --> 00:44:47.760
Isn't that right?

00:44:47.760 --> 00:44:52.940
Yes. I thought I'd keep some for whenever I open my own restaurant.

00:44:52.940 --> 00:44:57.150
I'm quite fond of wine, may I take a quick look?

00:44:57.150 --> 00:44:59.610
Certainly.

00:44:59.610 --> 00:45:00.530
Oww!

00:45:00.530 --> 00:45:02.530
The wood flooring is scratched up!

00:45:02.530 --> 00:45:06.070
Oh, are you all right? I dropped a bottle there the other day.

00:45:06.070 --> 00:45:09.120
Conan-<i>kun</i>. You're not wearing slippers, so be careful.

00:45:09.120 --> 00:45:12.000
Margaux, Lafite, Haut-Brion...

00:45:12.000 --> 00:45:14.960
Such an impressive collection of top-quality wine!

00:45:14.960 --> 00:45:17.710
That reminds me, what was it called again?

00:45:17.710 --> 00:45:21.340
Your treasured... Petr-?

00:45:21.340 --> 00:45:23.260
You have Chateau Petrus, too?!

00:45:23.260 --> 00:45:28.350
Chateau Petrus? That's what
Poirot drank in "Death on the Nile"!

00:45:28.350 --> 00:45:31.430
I did, but I drank it the other day.

00:45:31.430 --> 00:45:35.900
Huh?! But I thought it takes years until it's ready to drink?

00:45:35.900 --> 00:45:38.360
I just couldn't help myself.

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:42.280
Sawaki-<i>san</i>. We can talk wine another day.

00:45:42.280 --> 00:45:45.280
Can you tell us your plans for today?

00:45:45.280 --> 00:45:48.200
Do you know Asahi Katsuyoshi-<i>san</i>?

00:45:48.200 --> 00:45:53.290
He's a businessman who operates dozens of restaurants in the city.

00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:58.210
Oh, I've done a job for
Asahi-<i>san</i> in the past!

00:45:58.210 --> 00:46:04.470
I hear he's opening Aqua Crystal, that aquatic park in Tokyo Bay.

00:46:01.210 --> 00:46:04.130
"Asahi Katsuyoshi"

00:46:04.470 --> 00:46:09.600
Yes. He's offered to let me run a restaurant there,

00:46:09.600 --> 00:46:12.270
so I have a 3:00 appointment with him.

00:46:12.270 --> 00:46:14.310
Asahi Katsuyoshi?

00:46:14.310 --> 00:46:16.140
--Asahi?
--Hold on, now!

00:46:16.140 --> 00:46:18.850
Nine! There's a "nine" in "Asahi"!

00:46:16.690 --> 00:46:17.650
"Asahi"

00:46:17.650 --> 00:46:18.350
"Nine"

00:46:18.860 --> 00:46:22.610
Which means he's the next to be attacked.

00:46:22.610 --> 00:46:26.490
But he only hired me to find his pet cat.

00:46:26.490 --> 00:46:28.950
We're not really acquaintances...

00:46:28.950 --> 00:46:31.330
Murakami might not think so.

00:46:31.330 --> 00:46:35.410
In any event, let's protect Sawaki-<i>san</i> and meet with Asahi-<i>san</i>!

00:46:35.410 --> 00:46:37.210
Is that all right, Sawaki-<i>san</i>?

00:46:37.210 --> 00:46:40.000
Yes. I don't mind.

00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:41.800
Then you and Conan-<i>kun-</i>

00:46:41.800 --> 00:46:43.460
Are coming.

00:46:43.460 --> 00:46:45.550
Conan-<i>Kun</i> and I are coming, too!

00:46:45.550 --> 00:46:49.340
I've had enough of this, Ran!
This isn't a game!

00:46:49.340 --> 00:46:53.470
That's right! Lots of people are being attacked because of you!

00:46:53.470 --> 00:46:55.560
I can't just wait for my turn to come!

00:46:57.560 --> 00:46:58.770
Ran...

00:47:17.910 --> 00:47:20.210
That's Aqua Crystal?

00:47:20.210 --> 00:47:23.290
--My...
--What a flashy building...

00:47:31.550 --> 00:47:33.050
Reckless driver!

00:47:37.060 --> 00:47:40.900
A little bit off. But not too bad.

00:47:40.900 --> 00:47:43.610
Hey, you! That's dangerous, girly!

00:47:43.610 --> 00:47:46.070
--What is?
--Listen, you...

00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:54.580
Oh, Nana-<i>chan</i>! You too?

00:47:54.580 --> 00:47:58.330
Oh, Asahi-<i>san</i> invited you too, Shishido-<i>sensei</i>?!

00:47:58.330 --> 00:48:01.830
Pardon me, ma'am, but who are you?

00:48:01.830 --> 00:48:04.340
You don't know who I am, mister?!

00:48:04.340 --> 00:48:08.050
She's Osanai Nana-<i>san</i>, Inspector.
A popular model.

00:48:08.050 --> 00:48:10.930
Those three are from left to right-

00:48:10.930 --> 00:48:13.050
the essayist Nishina-<i>san,</i>

00:48:13.050 --> 00:48:15.720
the photographer
Shishido Eimei-<i>san</i>, and...

00:48:15.720 --> 00:48:17.270
Peter Ford.

00:48:17.270 --> 00:48:24.060
I take it you two are policemen?
And the famous Mori Kogoro-<i>san</i>?

00:48:24.060 --> 00:48:28.570
You're that famous detective?!

00:48:28.570 --> 00:48:31.490
I've never seen the real one before!
Shishido-<i>sensei</i>!

00:48:31.490 --> 00:48:33.320
--Take a picture!
--Peace!

00:48:35.070 --> 00:48:38.370
Oh, geez. Where'd that anger just now go?

00:48:38.370 --> 00:48:40.790
This is Sawaki Kohei-<i>san</i>, a sommelier,

00:48:40.790 --> 00:48:45.170
Mori-<i>san</i>'s daughter, Ran-<i>san,</i> and Edogawa Conan-<i>kun.</i>

00:48:45.170 --> 00:48:49.090
Oh, you're the "delicious book" girl.

00:48:49.090 --> 00:48:52.930
Wow! You remember me?!

00:48:52.930 --> 00:48:57.140
Beautiful wine and women always remain in people's hearts.

00:48:57.140 --> 00:48:58.890
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:48:58.890 --> 00:49:02.140
Have you all been asked here by Asahi-<i>san</i>?

00:49:02.140 --> 00:49:04.310
--Yes, for 3:00.
--I'm at 3:00, too!

00:49:04.310 --> 00:49:05.440
Same here.

00:49:05.440 --> 00:49:08.110
Inspector. Has there been some sort of incident?

00:49:08.110 --> 00:49:09.650
Yes, as a matter of fact...

00:49:09.650 --> 00:49:13.320
Hey, it's almost 3:00! Let's go already!

00:49:13.320 --> 00:49:17.280
Oh, right! Let's head to the restaurant for now!

00:49:17.280 --> 00:49:20.700
Huh? Come to think of it, all four people called here are-

00:49:22.000 --> 00:49:26.460
Is the monorail the only way to get to Aqua Crystal?

00:49:34.800 --> 00:49:36.510
Huh? There's no driver!

00:49:36.510 --> 00:49:39.140
It looks like you just need to press this button.

00:49:38.850 --> 00:49:40.260
"Start"

00:49:50.610 --> 00:49:52.940
This is quite something!

00:49:52.940 --> 00:49:57.660
A-are you not good with hanging in the air either, Nishina-<i>san</i>?

00:49:57.660 --> 00:50:02.330
No... It's water I'm afraid of.
I can't swim at all...

00:50:02.330 --> 00:50:07.250
Y-yeah, everyone has their little quirks.

00:50:07.250 --> 00:50:10.040
Even if it's a fact that your dad shot your mom,

00:50:10.040 --> 00:50:13.300
are you sure that equals the truth behind it?

00:50:57.760 --> 00:51:02.260
It's like an aquarium! This totally is an underwater restaurant!

00:51:04.390 --> 00:51:08.900
A Ferrari F40! How did they get it in here, I wonder!

00:51:08.900 --> 00:51:11.310
I don't seem to see Asahi-<i>san...</i>

00:51:11.310 --> 00:51:14.360
That's odd, after he invited guests here...

00:51:14.360 --> 00:51:16.650
Don't tell me Murakami already got to him?

00:51:16.650 --> 00:51:19.860
What does that mean?! "Murakami already got to him?"

00:51:19.860 --> 00:51:23.120
Oh, right! I need to tell you about that...

00:51:23.120 --> 00:51:25.870
Inspector. I'll go look around the place.

00:51:25.870 --> 00:51:28.160
--I'll come too.
--Alright.

00:51:28.160 --> 00:51:31.880
Okay, everyone! Just to be safe, please sit with your backs to the wall!

00:51:45.850 --> 00:51:48.140
So this is where the emergency exit is...

00:51:48.430 --> 00:51:50.900
"Wine Cellar"

00:51:54.110 --> 00:51:56.480
This is the only room that's locked...

00:51:57.570 --> 00:52:00.910
I see. So that's what's going on...

00:52:00.910 --> 00:52:03.570
Nothing out of the ordinary.

00:52:03.570 --> 00:52:06.200
Which means I could be "six".

00:52:06.200 --> 00:52:07.450
Why's that?

00:52:07.450 --> 00:52:10.870
The "shishi" in "Shishido" has a "six" in it.

00:52:10.870 --> 00:52:12.000
So it does!

00:52:12.000 --> 00:52:14.670
The other three have numbers in their names, too.

00:52:14.670 --> 00:52:15.420
What?

00:52:15.420 --> 00:52:17.590
Nana means "seven",

00:52:17.590 --> 00:52:19.090
"Nishina" has "two",

00:52:19.090 --> 00:52:22.390
and Ford has the English "four".

00:52:22.390 --> 00:52:23.680
Yeah...

00:52:23.680 --> 00:52:26.390
Now we just need a "three" and "one" to have all the numbers...

00:52:26.390 --> 00:52:29.850
I know of a "three".
He's right in front of you.

00:52:29.850 --> 00:52:31.270
Wait, you don't mean-

00:52:31.270 --> 00:52:34.770
My name is Shiratori Ninzaburo.

00:52:31.390 --> 00:52:34.520
"Shiratori Ninzaburo"
<i>(Zabu = three)</i>

00:52:34.770 --> 00:52:36.650
Ninzaburo?

00:52:36.650 --> 00:52:39.780
But there's definitely no "one" here...

00:52:39.780 --> 00:52:41.780
Shinichi.
<i>(Ichi = one)</i>

00:52:41.780 --> 00:52:45.370
Do you think Shinichi could be "one"?

00:52:45.370 --> 00:52:47.580
Is Kudo-<i>Kun</i> coming here?!

00:52:47.580 --> 00:52:51.210
No. But I just got that feeling...

00:52:51.210 --> 00:52:52.370
It's true;

00:52:52.370 --> 00:52:58.380
had I not shrunk, I would've been intrigued enough to come too!

00:52:58.380 --> 00:53:02.050
Does that mean "one" does refer to me?

00:53:02.280 --> 00:53:07.120
Tell me, are any of you connected with Murakami Joe in any way?

00:53:07.120 --> 00:53:09.790
Of course I'm not!

00:53:09.790 --> 00:53:11.120
Me neither!

00:53:11.120 --> 00:53:13.120
I am.

00:53:13.120 --> 00:53:17.250
Before I became an essayist, I was a criminal investigative reporter,

00:53:17.250 --> 00:53:20.050
and I had done a report on the Murakami incident.

00:53:20.050 --> 00:53:21.760
I'm connected, too.

00:53:21.760 --> 00:53:26.890
I photographed him for a photo album called "Portraits of Criminals".

00:53:26.890 --> 00:53:28.970
Did any trouble occur at the time?

00:53:28.970 --> 00:53:30.930
Nothing at all.

00:53:34.310 --> 00:53:35.900
What is it, Nana-<i>san</i>?

00:53:35.900 --> 00:53:39.570
He got out of prison eight days ago, right?

00:53:39.570 --> 00:53:40.650
Yes.

00:53:40.650 --> 00:53:43.360
Then it's unrelated.

00:53:43.360 --> 00:53:48.530
Oh, you guys! Getting all serious!
Let's quit talking about this!

00:53:48.530 --> 00:53:51.120
More importantly, aren't you the one

00:53:51.120 --> 00:53:54.330
who wrote that lame book, "Restaurants in Paris"?!

00:53:54.330 --> 00:53:58.290
All the restaurants you recommended in it sucked!

00:53:58.290 --> 00:54:00.880
--Do you even understand tastes?!
--How rude!

00:54:00.880 --> 00:54:03.010
Of course I do!

00:54:03.010 --> 00:54:05.130
Then let's see some proof.

00:54:05.130 --> 00:54:05.970
Proof?

00:54:05.970 --> 00:54:09.140
I brought this as a gift for Asahi-<i>san,</i>

00:54:09.140 --> 00:54:12.350
but let's see you guess what wine this is!

00:54:12.350 --> 00:54:15.730
Blind tasting, huh? All right, then.

00:54:26.700 --> 00:54:29.160
This elegant, violet fragrance...

00:54:29.160 --> 00:54:31.660
This velvety texture going down...

00:54:31.660 --> 00:54:37.710
Chambertin, the beloved drink of Napoleon, Emperor of the French.

00:54:37.710 --> 00:54:39.630
I got you!

00:54:39.630 --> 00:54:43.670
As if I'd ever buy something that cheap as a gift for someone!

00:54:43.670 --> 00:54:45.210
Then what is this?!

00:54:47.550 --> 00:54:50.260
--You're a sommelier.
--Yes.

00:54:50.260 --> 00:54:53.680
Tell this fraud of an essayist the answer.

00:55:13.370 --> 00:55:15.750
Moulin-à-Vent, Beaujolais, yes?

00:55:15.750 --> 00:55:16.950
Correct!

00:55:16.950 --> 00:55:19.330
No way! This is a Beaujolais?!

00:55:19.330 --> 00:55:23.090
High-quality Beaujolais, when left to age for a long time,

00:55:23.090 --> 00:55:26.760
can produce top-quality
Bourgogne-like flavors and fragrances.

00:55:26.760 --> 00:55:32.760
Now do you get it? I suggest you call it quits as a "gourmet essayist"!

00:55:34.850 --> 00:55:37.850
Now I feel like having some wine, too!

00:55:37.850 --> 00:55:40.770
Let's all have some, then!
I'll get the stuff!

00:55:40.770 --> 00:55:43.270
I'll have some beer. Where's the kitchen?

00:55:43.270 --> 00:55:44.400
That way.

00:55:44.400 --> 00:55:46.650
Alright! Lead the way, brat!

00:55:46.650 --> 00:55:47.900
Okay!

00:55:47.900 --> 00:55:49.950
Who're you callin' a brat?!

00:55:51.570 --> 00:55:53.620
Ah! Here we go!

00:55:53.620 --> 00:55:56.040
Good news, brat! There's juice here, too!

00:55:56.040 --> 00:55:57.910
Really?! I'm so happy!

00:55:57.910 --> 00:55:59.580
Enough with the brat stuff!

00:56:04.750 --> 00:56:06.800
Here, Ran-<i>neechan</i>!

00:56:06.800 --> 00:56:09.170
Thanks!

00:56:09.170 --> 00:56:10.300
Oops!

00:56:11.430 --> 00:56:15.180
It really is as delicious as you say, Sawaki-<i>san</i>!

00:56:15.180 --> 00:56:17.010
Sawaki-<i>san</i>! How about another glass?

00:56:17.010 --> 00:56:20.100
Oh, no, thank you.
I'll have some mineral water.

00:56:20.100 --> 00:56:21.480
Thanks!

00:56:21.480 --> 00:56:23.190
You're not having beer?

00:56:23.190 --> 00:56:28.150
Of course not! There's no telling when Murakami could strike!

00:56:28.150 --> 00:56:30.740
Here you are, Inspector!

00:56:30.740 --> 00:56:32.990
Here, Conan-<i>kun</i>. You can have mine.

00:56:32.990 --> 00:56:35.660
T-that's okay! I'll get another one!

00:56:35.660 --> 00:56:38.580
Hey! Don't be scampering around, now!

00:56:47.710 --> 00:56:51.380
The mineral water is in the bottom drawer of the fridge!

00:56:51.380 --> 00:56:53.010
Oh, thanks.

00:56:53.010 --> 00:56:56.640
I saw a rare seasoning here, so I gave it a taste.

00:56:56.640 --> 00:56:59.520
--Is your juice up here, Conan-<i>kun</i>?
--Yeah!

00:57:02.560 --> 00:57:07.150
What's taking Asahi-<i>san</i> so long?
What could he be up to?!

00:57:10.360 --> 00:57:13.240
W-what's going on?! What's wrong?!

00:57:15.280 --> 00:57:16.990
Just joking!

00:57:16.990 --> 00:57:18.660
Ugh...

00:57:18.660 --> 00:57:22.250
Ford-<i>san</i>! Please don't joke around at a time like this!

00:57:24.120 --> 00:57:28.710
Incidentally, why are you all here today, anyway?

00:57:28.710 --> 00:57:31.510
I got a call from his secretary.

00:57:31.510 --> 00:57:36.140
Said Asahi-<i>san</i> was a fan of mine and wanted to meet with me.

00:57:36.140 --> 00:57:40.390
Maybe he wants me to help promote this place or something?

00:57:40.390 --> 00:57:43.140
I also received a call from his secretary.

00:57:43.140 --> 00:57:45.230
I got the same invitation.

00:57:45.230 --> 00:57:48.520
I even got a present from him!

00:57:48.520 --> 00:57:50.230
Here! This nail polish!

00:57:50.230 --> 00:57:53.490
It's made in France and super expensive!

00:57:53.490 --> 00:57:57.240
--You too, Nishina-<i>san</i>?
--Yeah, me too!

00:57:57.240 --> 00:57:59.580
What're you doing there, Nana-<i>chan</i>?

00:57:59.580 --> 00:58:03.080
I drew on the wine cork with nail polish! Isn't it cute?

00:58:03.080 --> 00:58:05.620
What is it? A raccoon dog?!

00:58:05.620 --> 00:58:09.250
Oh, you're such a meanie! It's a cat!

00:58:09.250 --> 00:58:13.050
Sawaki-<i>san</i>. This is addressed to you.
I found it on the ground.

00:58:15.260 --> 00:58:17.180
"Sawaki Kohei-<i>san..."</i>

00:58:17.180 --> 00:58:21.430
"I may be late, so please treat everyone to any bottle of wine you want

00:58:21.430 --> 00:58:26.060
from Rack M-18 in the wine cellar."

00:58:26.060 --> 00:58:29.940
"The key is in an envelope on the checkout counter."

00:58:29.940 --> 00:58:34.110
"Thanks. -Asahi Katsuyoshi"

00:58:34.110 --> 00:58:38.700
Was that paper there when I picked up the juice earlier?

00:58:38.700 --> 00:58:41.580
Hey! I wanna see the wine cellar!

00:58:41.580 --> 00:58:42.910
Me too!

00:58:42.910 --> 00:58:46.370
I'd like to see what wine there is, too!

00:58:46.370 --> 00:58:48.540
Then let's all go together!

00:58:59.390 --> 00:59:02.300
--My word!
--What a sight!

00:59:02.300 --> 00:59:06.140
--It's cool in here...
--No, it's almost too warm!

00:59:06.140 --> 00:59:12.150
A temperature between 10° to 14° C is ideal for preserving wine,

00:59:12.150 --> 00:59:16.150
but it's up to 17° C in here.

00:59:16.150 --> 00:59:19.530
Just look at these, Inspector!
They're all rare wines!

00:59:19.530 --> 00:59:23.990
Romanee-Conti, La Tache, Le Pin,
Cote-Rotie, Clos du Mesnil...

00:59:23.990 --> 00:59:25.290
Just amazing!

00:59:25.290 --> 00:59:29.000
Shelf M-18...

00:59:29.000 --> 00:59:30.170
There it is!

00:59:30.170 --> 00:59:31.250
Look out!

00:59:33.790 --> 00:59:35.460
A booby-trap!

00:59:35.460 --> 00:59:37.380
Mister! Inspector!

00:59:40.300 --> 00:59:43.220
This is just like the one that hit me in the side!

00:59:43.220 --> 00:59:44.640
Inspector!

00:59:44.640 --> 00:59:47.020
The crossbow is set up here!

00:59:47.020 --> 00:59:49.230
An 8 of Spades...

00:59:49.230 --> 00:59:53.360
So it was Murakami who set this up, and wrote that letter!

00:59:53.360 --> 00:59:57.900
If so, why would he skip nine and go after Sawaki-<i>san</i>, who's eight?

00:59:59.030 --> 01:00:00.240
It couldn't be!

01:00:00.240 --> 01:00:03.950
Inspector! Let's evacuate from this building for the time being!

01:00:08.830 --> 01:00:12.880
Huh? It's closed.
Was the entrance not here?

01:00:12.880 --> 01:00:14.340
No, this is the place.

01:00:14.340 --> 01:00:17.050
If we're leaving, can I get my coat first?

01:00:17.050 --> 01:00:18.340
Go ahead.

01:00:29.600 --> 01:00:30.680
Asahi-<i>san</i>!

01:00:30.680 --> 01:00:33.190
The 9 of Spades! It was Murakami!

01:00:33.190 --> 01:00:36.480
Inspector! I can't open this door, it has an electronic lock!

01:00:36.480 --> 01:00:39.190
What?! Alright, I'll call for help!

01:00:38.530 --> 01:00:40.940
"No Service"

01:00:39.190 --> 01:00:40.940
No good! We're out of service range!

01:00:42.450 --> 01:00:44.870
It's been cut! Damn it!

01:00:44.870 --> 01:00:47.580
Inspector! I'm gonna check the emergency exit!

01:00:53.210 --> 01:00:54.250
What?!

01:00:54.250 --> 01:00:56.840
It's blocked with cement!

01:00:58.170 --> 01:01:02.220
This is your fault! We have nothing to do with this!

01:01:02.220 --> 01:01:04.550
Yeah! What do you have to say for yourself?!

01:01:06.970 --> 01:01:10.770
The fact Murakami didn't go out of numerical order

01:01:10.770 --> 01:01:14.480
means you're next, Nana-<i>chan</i>!

01:01:14.480 --> 01:01:16.360
Q-quit it!

01:01:16.360 --> 01:01:20.280
Why do I have to be targeted by some man I've never even heard of?!

01:01:20.280 --> 01:01:22.860
But something bugs you, right?

01:01:22.860 --> 01:01:24.490
Earlier, you...

01:01:24.490 --> 01:01:27.910
He got out of prison eight days ago, right?

01:01:27.910 --> 01:01:29.410
Yes.

01:01:29.410 --> 01:01:32.250
I already told you, it was unrelated!

01:01:32.250 --> 01:01:37.420
We will determine if it's unrelated or not. Please talk to us.

01:01:39.420 --> 01:01:41.590
Three months ago...

01:01:45.800 --> 01:01:48.100
Apparently!

01:02:05.030 --> 01:02:08.990
We didn't collide, but I got scared and drove off!

01:02:08.990 --> 01:02:11.700
Did the person have an off-road motorcycle?!

01:02:11.700 --> 01:02:14.540
No, it was a regular motorcycle.

01:02:14.540 --> 01:02:19.380
Inspector. Nana-<i>san</i> is right.
It's unrelated to what's happening now.

01:02:19.380 --> 01:02:22.170
More importantly, we need to figure a way out of here!

01:02:22.170 --> 01:02:26.590
Yeah. We might find an exit if we search the entire building.

01:02:26.590 --> 01:02:30.180
Then let's split up and look, too.

01:02:30.180 --> 01:02:31.970
Guess there's no other choice.

01:02:31.970 --> 01:02:34.480
Listen! Ran and Conan, you stay here!

01:02:34.480 --> 01:02:37.020
You remain here too, Nana-<i>san</i>!

01:02:37.020 --> 01:02:38.310
Okay...

01:03:06.590 --> 01:03:11.010
What's taking everyone so long?
Can't they find an exit?

01:03:11.010 --> 01:03:15.180
Don't worry! I'm sure they'll find one and be right back!

01:03:15.180 --> 01:03:17.230
I'll just do some searching, too!

01:03:20.520 --> 01:03:23.110
You were told to stay here!

01:03:23.110 --> 01:03:26.240
Honestly! You're so curious about everything...

01:03:26.240 --> 01:03:27.690
But!

01:03:33.120 --> 01:03:34.160
A power outage?!

01:03:34.160 --> 01:03:36.750
What?! What's going on?!
Why are the lights out?!

01:03:36.750 --> 01:03:38.040
Luminescent paint!

01:03:42.630 --> 01:03:45.090
--Help!
--Stay there, Nana-<i>san</i>!

01:03:45.090 --> 01:03:46.920
Don't tell me this blackout-

01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:51.890
What?! What happened?!

01:03:51.890 --> 01:03:54.970
--What was that scream?!
--Inspector!

01:03:54.970 --> 01:03:57.890
--Mori-<i>Kun</i>! The electrical room!
--Right!

01:03:57.890 --> 01:03:59.230
Nana-<i>san</i>?!

01:04:03.940 --> 01:04:05.860
Is this it?

01:04:09.490 --> 01:04:10.900
Nana-<i>san</i>!

01:04:15.240 --> 01:04:17.290
What the-?!

01:04:17.290 --> 01:04:19.250
--Nana-<i>san</i>!
--Move aside!

01:04:20.210 --> 01:04:21.580
She's dead!

01:04:21.580 --> 01:04:24.130
The 7 of Spades, and a Joker...

01:04:24.130 --> 01:04:27.920
It's Murakami! Murakami's here, inside this building!

01:04:27.920 --> 01:04:29.050
Damn it!

01:04:29.050 --> 01:04:30.470
I'll go check around!

01:04:30.470 --> 01:04:33.470
Mori-<i>san</i>! It's dangerous to go alone! I'll come with you!

01:04:35.010 --> 01:04:36.470
Shishido-<i>san.</i>

01:04:36.470 --> 01:04:38.810
Please cease your photography.

01:04:38.810 --> 01:04:40.270
Why's that?

01:04:40.270 --> 01:04:44.270
Since help can't come right away, you'll have to do the autopsy,

01:04:44.270 --> 01:04:48.440
but won't you need to photograph the scene of the crime first?

01:04:48.440 --> 01:04:50.320
Y-you have a point...

01:04:50.320 --> 01:04:53.660
Then I expect you to hand them over to the police later on.

01:04:53.660 --> 01:04:56.070
Yes, but of course!

01:04:58.160 --> 01:05:02.830
But how did Murakami manage to do this in pitch darkness?

01:05:02.830 --> 01:05:06.590
Luminescent paint.
Nana-<i>san</i>'s fingernails were glowing.

01:05:06.590 --> 01:05:08.000
What?!

01:05:08.000 --> 01:05:13.760
I see! Luminescent paint was added to the nail polish she was given!

01:05:19.310 --> 01:05:21.180
Her middle nail...

01:05:21.180 --> 01:05:25.480
Hey, Inspector!
Nana-<i>san</i>'s left fingernail is weird!

01:05:25.480 --> 01:05:29.400
The nail polish came off!
Or, wait... did her nail break off?

01:05:29.400 --> 01:05:32.360
I think that's a press-on nail that came off.

01:05:32.360 --> 01:05:33.530
Press-on?

01:05:33.530 --> 01:05:35.490
They're not real fingernails.

01:05:35.490 --> 01:05:39.870
They come in various designs, and you glue them to your nails.

01:05:39.870 --> 01:05:46.170
Oh? So it came off by chance, then?

01:05:46.170 --> 01:05:48.210
Here we are!

01:05:48.210 --> 01:05:50.840
It doesn't seem related to her murder...

01:05:50.840 --> 01:05:52.510
Oh...

01:05:54.970 --> 01:06:00.470
She was grabbed with a left hand! 
And pretty forcefully, at that!

01:06:00.470 --> 01:06:03.560
Which means... the killer is right-handed!

01:06:03.560 --> 01:06:08.520
If I remember right, Murakami... is left-handed!

01:06:08.520 --> 01:06:11.650
It wasn't MuraKami who killed Nana-san!

01:06:11.650 --> 01:06:15.030
Wait a minute! A while back, the Killer...

01:06:15.030 --> 01:06:17.570
Think back! Remember!

01:06:20.990 --> 01:06:22.450
He's right-handed!

01:06:22.450 --> 01:06:26.580
What the hell?! I've been making a huge mistake this whole time!

01:06:29.290 --> 01:06:32.550
Inspector! No luck!
Murakami's nowhere to be found!

01:06:32.550 --> 01:06:35.130
Could he have already escaped?

01:06:35.130 --> 01:06:37.880
That can't be! There's no way out!

01:06:37.880 --> 01:06:40.850
He must be hiding somewhere still!

01:06:40.850 --> 01:06:45.520
No... MuraKami isn't the killer.
It's someone in here!

01:06:45.520 --> 01:06:48.690
Who?! Who killed Nana-san?!

01:06:48.690 --> 01:06:50.900
Come to think of it, the killer...

01:06:53.530 --> 01:06:56.490
...kicked the can of juice
I left on the floor!

01:07:00.030 --> 01:07:02.580
The contents have spilled onto the floor.

01:07:02.580 --> 01:07:06.750
I'm certain there was about half left in it when I set it down.

01:07:06.750 --> 01:07:09.670
So if the killer kicked the can...

01:07:09.670 --> 01:07:15.130
...the juice must've flown out and stained the killer's pants!

01:07:15.130 --> 01:07:18.550
Nana-san's killer is one of these four men!

01:07:26.640 --> 01:07:30.150
Him?! But why?!

01:07:30.150 --> 01:07:34.780
I'm sorry, Sawaki-<i>san.</i>
Because of me, Asahi-<i>san</i> was murdered,

01:07:34.780 --> 01:07:37.490
and you never got to discuss running his restaurant...

01:07:37.490 --> 01:07:41.740
Not at all. I was going to turn him down, anyway.

01:07:41.740 --> 01:07:47.040
Actually, I've decided to quit my current job and return to the country.

01:07:47.040 --> 01:07:52.670
I'm an only son, so I need to take care of my parents.

01:07:52.670 --> 01:07:56.170
In any case, we'd be wise not to act rashly now.

01:07:56.170 --> 01:07:57.510
Especially you, Shishido-<i>san.</i>

01:07:57.510 --> 01:08:04.100
Yeah, I know. I'm next, right?
I'll be extra careful not to get killed.

01:08:04.100 --> 01:08:09.100
Inspector! I refuse to die!
I will get out of here alive!

01:08:09.100 --> 01:08:12.400
Wait a minute! Could it be that he...

01:08:32.790 --> 01:08:34.500
What're you up to now?!

01:08:34.500 --> 01:08:37.050
I thought everyone might be thirsty...

01:08:37.050 --> 01:08:40.470
You idiot! Don't be running around on your own!

01:08:40.470 --> 01:08:43.390
There's no telling where
Murakami might be hiding!

01:08:43.390 --> 01:08:46.510
But there's no number in my name, so...

01:08:46.510 --> 01:08:47.470
Yeesh!

01:08:47.470 --> 01:08:49.390
Here you go!

01:08:49.390 --> 01:08:51.560
Here you go, Sawaki-<i>san</i>!

01:08:51.560 --> 01:08:52.270
Thank you.

01:08:52.270 --> 01:08:54.060
Hey, brat! Gimme some too!

01:08:54.060 --> 01:08:55.360
Sure!

01:08:57.320 --> 01:08:59.990
Japanese water really is delicious!

01:09:02.200 --> 01:09:03.490
That's great!

01:09:03.490 --> 01:09:05.910
I was right! No doubt about it!

01:09:05.910 --> 01:09:08.080
But there's no proof.

01:09:08.080 --> 01:09:10.410
Come to think of it, where is it?!

01:09:21.880 --> 01:09:24.180
I found the proof!

01:09:29.810 --> 01:09:31.060
What was that?!

01:09:31.060 --> 01:09:32.770
There appears to have been an explosion somewhere!

01:09:32.770 --> 01:09:35.560
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>! Shishido-<i>san</i> is next! Protect Shishido-<i>san</i>!

01:09:35.560 --> 01:09:36.270
Yes, sir!

01:09:36.270 --> 01:09:40.110
Shishido-<i>san</i>!
Where are you, Shishido-<i>san</i>?!

01:09:40.110 --> 01:09:42.110
--Right here.
--Put that out!

01:09:42.110 --> 01:09:43.950
Do you want to die?!

01:09:47.370 --> 01:09:50.910
I'm "two", so I won't get attacked for a long time!

01:09:53.080 --> 01:09:55.170
Sawaki-<i>san</i>! Are you hurt?!

01:09:55.170 --> 01:09:58.210
N-no. Do you suppose
I'll be targeted again?

01:09:58.210 --> 01:10:00.880
I-I'm not sure...

01:10:00.880 --> 01:10:03.090
Thank you! Emergency lights!

01:10:09.600 --> 01:10:11.060
W-what the?!

01:10:14.560 --> 01:10:17.770
H-h-help! I can't swi-!

01:10:36.460 --> 01:10:38.210
Here, grab on!

01:10:41.590 --> 01:10:44.460
Heya, brat! Glad to see you're alive!

01:10:48.090 --> 01:10:51.430
Huh?! Ran! Where are you?! Ran!

01:10:51.430 --> 01:10:52.640
Don't tell me she's...

01:10:56.180 --> 01:10:58.440
Wait, Conan! Where are you going?!

01:10:58.440 --> 01:11:00.190
Ran! Where are you?!

01:11:08.280 --> 01:11:09.410
Ran!

01:11:16.540 --> 01:11:20.880
Ran! Everything's okay now! Calm down!

01:11:20.880 --> 01:11:23.670
S-Shinichi?

01:11:25.340 --> 01:11:26.970
Conan-kun!

01:11:33.220 --> 01:11:34.680
It's no good!

01:11:34.680 --> 01:11:37.390
Oh, yeah! My Elasticity Suspenders!

01:11:39.190 --> 01:11:41.230
Crap! My leg's stuck!

01:11:41.230 --> 01:11:44.480
Dammit! Oh no! Can't breathe!

01:12:02.790 --> 01:12:04.340
R-Ran!

01:12:09.840 --> 01:12:11.760
Hey! Ran! Ran!

01:12:11.760 --> 01:12:13.010
Damn it!

01:12:16.890 --> 01:12:19.230
I'm free! I gotta hurry!

01:12:58.810 --> 01:13:01.520
Hey! Ran! Ran! Say something!

01:13:05.150 --> 01:13:08.530
D-Dad...

01:13:08.530 --> 01:13:11.610
Thank Conan.

01:13:13.110 --> 01:13:15.620
Thank you, Conan-<i>kun...</i>

01:13:16.490 --> 01:13:19.910
No, uhh...

01:13:19.910 --> 01:13:21.000
What's wrong?!

01:13:21.000 --> 01:13:23.920
I seem to have reopened my wound!

01:13:23.920 --> 01:13:25.250
What?!

01:13:25.250 --> 01:13:27.170
Look! Over there!

01:13:27.170 --> 01:13:29.210
The 6 to 2 of Spades!

01:13:29.210 --> 01:13:33.680
Damn it! Is he planning to kill us all at once here?! Screw that!

01:13:33.680 --> 01:13:38.180
But, at this rate, it is going to happen.
Because there's no way out!

01:13:38.180 --> 01:13:40.100
--I know a way out!
--What?!

01:13:40.100 --> 01:13:42.350
You know, the exploded windows!

01:13:42.350 --> 01:13:46.270
Yeah! We can go into the sea through them!

01:13:46.270 --> 01:13:48.940
N-no! I can't!

01:13:48.940 --> 01:13:52.110
Quit bein' a sissy! I'll take you with me!

01:13:52.110 --> 01:13:53.950
Then I'll take you, little boy!

01:13:53.950 --> 01:13:56.280
I'll be fine by myself!

01:13:56.280 --> 01:14:00.160
And I'll take you. Think you got a little bit left in you?!

01:14:01.290 --> 01:14:03.200
--I'll help you, Inspector.
--Thanks...

01:14:03.200 --> 01:14:06.000
Then I'll lead the way! Let's go!

01:14:08.210 --> 01:14:11.050
Here we go! Deep breath!

01:14:12.550 --> 01:14:14.970
Hold on tight and don't let go now!

01:14:14.970 --> 01:14:16.380
R-right!

01:14:50.080 --> 01:14:52.090
Here! Grab my hand!

01:14:59.840 --> 01:15:01.760
--Take Ran!
--Right!

01:15:07.850 --> 01:15:10.480
We're saved, aren't we?

01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:12.820
Yes. We're safe now!

01:15:14.280 --> 01:15:16.360
Nishina! Nishina!

01:15:16.360 --> 01:15:18.070
Hey! Say something!

01:15:18.070 --> 01:15:23.080
I'll give him CPR!
I'm a certified lifeguard!

01:15:23.080 --> 01:15:28.830
Hold it! Detective Shiratori!
You give him CPR!

01:15:28.830 --> 01:15:31.540
Huh? No, I didn't say anything-

01:15:31.540 --> 01:15:34.210
Do it now, Shiratori!

01:15:34.210 --> 01:15:35.760
Understood!

01:15:40.890 --> 01:15:42.430
Huh?

01:15:47.140 --> 01:15:48.390
Mori-<i>Kun</i>?

01:15:48.390 --> 01:15:49.480
Inspector!

01:15:49.480 --> 01:15:53.570
The person behind this string of incidents is not Murakami Joe!

01:15:53.570 --> 01:15:55.020
Say what?!

01:15:55.020 --> 01:16:00.110
Because the person who shot
Dr. Agasa and killed Nana-<i>san</i>

01:16:00.110 --> 01:16:01.860
was right-handed!

01:16:01.860 --> 01:16:03.370
Right-handed?!

01:16:04.450 --> 01:16:06.290
Y-you're all right!

01:16:08.500 --> 01:16:13.290
The real culprit most likely met Murakami after he was released,

01:16:13.290 --> 01:16:16.210
learned things from him, like how I shot him 10 years ago

01:16:16.210 --> 01:16:21.800
and that he was once a gambling dealer nicknamed "Joker",

01:16:21.800 --> 01:16:24.350
and decided to use him.

01:16:24.350 --> 01:16:25.260
Use?

01:16:25.260 --> 01:16:31.560
Yes. The killer realized that he and the people he wanted to kill

01:16:31.560 --> 01:16:35.570
all had numbers in their names.

01:16:35.570 --> 01:16:40.490
So he came up with the idea of combining these "name numbers"

01:16:40.490 --> 01:16:44.910
with playing cards to pin his crimes on Murakami.

01:16:44.910 --> 01:16:48.660
Then the reason Eri-<i>san,</i>
Dr. Agasa, and I were attacked

01:16:48.660 --> 01:16:50.580
was to act as camouflage to make us think

01:16:50.580 --> 01:16:52.790
Murakami was getting revenge against you?!

01:16:52.790 --> 01:16:54.380
That's right.

01:16:54.380 --> 01:16:57.880
Then who did the culprit really want to kill?!

01:16:57.880 --> 01:17:00.760
Asahi-<i>san</i> and Nana-<i>san.</i>

01:17:00.760 --> 01:17:02.340
And Tsuji-<i>san.</i>

01:17:02.340 --> 01:17:05.720
Given that the method used against him switching his eyedrops-

01:17:05.720 --> 01:17:11.770
had a very high probability of being fatal, there's likely no doubt.

01:17:11.770 --> 01:17:13.900
Mori-<i>Kun</i>! Who is the killer, then?!

01:17:13.900 --> 01:17:16.400
The killer is among us.

01:17:16.400 --> 01:17:17.820
What?!

01:17:20.070 --> 01:17:23.820
Come to think of it, didn't Nana-<i>san</i> humiliate you?

01:17:23.820 --> 01:17:26.030
N-no! I didn't kill her!

01:17:26.030 --> 01:17:29.580
That's right. You were to be killed.

01:17:29.580 --> 01:17:32.460
As you can't swim, the killer attempted to drown you

01:17:32.460 --> 01:17:36.460
by blowing up the underwater restaurant.

01:17:36.460 --> 01:17:38.290
Say, Detective Shiratori.

01:17:38.290 --> 01:17:43.930
When you gave CPR to Nishina-<i>san,</i> what was the first thing you did?

01:17:43.930 --> 01:17:45.300
What did I do?

01:17:45.300 --> 01:17:48.220
You're supposed to tilt the head back, lift the throat up,

01:17:48.220 --> 01:17:50.560
and keep the airway open!

01:17:50.560 --> 01:17:54.060
Then, what would happen if you hadn't kept the airway open,

01:17:54.060 --> 01:17:58.230
and only pretended to give CPR, while shutting the nose and mouth?

01:17:58.230 --> 01:18:01.570
That'd kill him, obviously!

01:18:02.900 --> 01:18:04.820
Y-you're not saying...

01:18:04.820 --> 01:18:08.410
Yes. The person who murdered
Asahi-<i>san</i> and Nana-<i>san</i>

01:18:08.410 --> 01:18:11.620
and tried to kill
Tsuji-<i>san</i> and Nishina-<i>san...</i>

01:18:11.620 --> 01:18:15.420
It was you, Sawaki Kohei-<i>san</i>!

01:18:15.420 --> 01:18:18.630
Mori-<i>san</i>! I was attacked with a crossbow too, you know!

01:18:18.630 --> 01:18:22.130
You had set that up beforehand.

01:18:22.130 --> 01:18:27.890
After you murdered Asahi-<i>san</i> here last night, that is!

01:18:27.890 --> 01:18:31.060
Then the letter that was under the table...

01:18:31.060 --> 01:18:33.770
And the secretary that called us all...

01:18:33.770 --> 01:18:35.600
Sawaki-<i>san</i> was behind it all.

01:18:35.600 --> 01:18:40.270
Including Nana-<i>san</i>'s luminescent nail polish, of course!

01:18:40.270 --> 01:18:42.780
Motive! What was his motive?!

01:18:44.150 --> 01:18:48.160
Something to do with ageusia, most likely.

01:18:48.160 --> 01:18:50.660
Ageusia?

01:18:50.660 --> 01:18:54.500
That's when you can't taste food and drinks anymore, right?

01:18:54.500 --> 01:18:58.420
Yes. He suffers from this ageusia.

01:19:02.170 --> 01:19:08.930
Apparently, ageusia is caused by stress or external head injuries.

01:19:08.930 --> 01:19:10.510
External head injuries?

01:19:10.510 --> 01:19:15.140
Then Sawaki-<i>san</i> was the person
Nana-<i>san</i> got in an accident with?!

01:19:15.140 --> 01:19:17.140
H-h-hold on now!

01:19:17.140 --> 01:19:19.440
You claim he lost his sense of taste,

01:19:19.440 --> 01:19:23.150
but he named Nana-<i>san</i>'s wine brand correctly!

01:19:23.150 --> 01:19:27.820
He could tell the brand by the wine's color and scent alone.

01:19:27.820 --> 01:19:29.160
That's possible?

01:19:29.160 --> 01:19:33.370
After it happened,
Sawaki-<i>san</i> continued as a sommelier,

01:19:33.370 --> 01:19:36.040
relying on vision and smell alone.

01:19:36.040 --> 01:19:42.380
But it was an affront to his aesthetic desire to be a perfect sommelier.

01:19:42.380 --> 01:19:47.090
That's why he decided to leave his position and return to the country.

01:19:47.090 --> 01:19:50.720
But not before getting revenge on Nana-<i>san</i> and everyone else

01:19:50.720 --> 01:19:54.350
who had caused him to lose his sense of taste!

01:19:55.350 --> 01:19:58.230
It must have been quite hard to accept.

01:19:58.230 --> 01:20:02.980
Enough to make him break the bottle of wine he treasured and saved

01:20:02.980 --> 01:20:07.240
for the day he would finally open his own restaurant.

01:20:07.240 --> 01:20:10.820
Then that mark on his floor was-

01:20:10.820 --> 01:20:14.120
But how did you manage to figure all this out?

01:20:14.120 --> 01:20:18.250
Yes. It was because he tried to taste some seasoning.

01:20:18.250 --> 01:20:24.750
What he tried was chili powder.

01:20:24.750 --> 01:20:27.920
People like sommeliers who use their tongues for a living

01:20:27.920 --> 01:20:32.050
don't put irritants or stimulants in their mouths, you see.

01:20:32.050 --> 01:20:37.010
I was able to confirm that he had lost his sense of taste

01:20:37.010 --> 01:20:40.520
when I had Conan give him some mineral water.

01:20:40.520 --> 01:20:42.520
Mineral water?

01:20:42.520 --> 01:20:48.280
The glass that Conan gave you had salt in it.

01:20:48.280 --> 01:20:52.240
And I drank it without realizing it?

01:20:52.240 --> 01:20:55.580
It's true that I suffer from ageusia.

01:20:55.580 --> 01:21:01.290
But that hardly proves that I murdered Nana-<i>san.</i>

01:21:01.290 --> 01:21:06.840
But there is proof. In either your left or right jacket pocket.

01:21:12.550 --> 01:21:15.390
That's the cork Nana-<i>san</i> drew on!

01:21:15.390 --> 01:21:19.520
Nana-<i>san</i> had that cork on her until just before she was murdered.

01:21:19.520 --> 01:21:23.190
So what was it doing in your pocket?

01:21:23.190 --> 01:21:27.360
It's because when you stabbed her from behind,

01:21:27.360 --> 01:21:29.400
Nana-<i>san</i> spun around and grabbed at you,

01:21:29.400 --> 01:21:33.320
at which time the cork slipped inside your pocket!

01:21:33.320 --> 01:21:38.160
The press-on nail on the floor likely came off at this time.

01:21:38.160 --> 01:21:44.670
How ironic that a wine cork should prove a sommelier's crime.

01:21:44.670 --> 01:21:46.540
But there's one more thing!

01:21:46.540 --> 01:21:51.630
And it's most likely still asleep in one of your pockets!

01:21:55.090 --> 01:21:59.680
The final Ace of Spades that matches those there.

01:21:59.680 --> 01:22:02.310
The card for Kudo Shinichi!

01:22:05.060 --> 01:22:06.900
The Ace of Spades!

01:22:17.620 --> 01:22:21.540
Mori-<i>san</i>. It's all as you say.

01:22:21.540 --> 01:22:25.000
Three months ago, on my way home from the restaurant,

01:22:25.000 --> 01:22:29.500
I nearly collided with her car, and fell off my motorcycle.

01:22:29.500 --> 01:22:34.340
A while after, I suddenly lost all sense of taste.

01:22:34.340 --> 01:22:38.890
The doctor said stress might also be the cause.

01:22:38.890 --> 01:22:43.180
Having lost all hope, I decided to give up being a sommelier

01:22:43.180 --> 01:22:45.850
and enact revenge on the cause of the accident, Osanai Nana,

01:22:45.850 --> 01:22:51.190
and the causes of my stress,
Asahi, Tsuji, and Nishina.

01:22:52.360 --> 01:22:55.740
But what did Asahi-<i>san</i> and the others do to you?!

01:22:55.740 --> 01:23:00.700
Asahi caught wind of a "wine boom" and used his vast fortune

01:23:00.700 --> 01:23:03.200
to buy up all the rare foreign wine available!

01:23:03.200 --> 01:23:05.620
And he couldn't even take care of it right!

01:23:05.620 --> 01:23:09.920
Nishina! You pretended to be a gourmet, wrote know-it-all books,

01:23:09.920 --> 01:23:13.550
and planted incorrect information about wine in readers' minds!

01:23:13.550 --> 01:23:15.670
And Tsuji Hiroki!

01:23:15.670 --> 01:23:19.680
He sullied my dignity as a sommelier!

01:23:19.680 --> 01:23:24.770
Four months ago, I attended a party he held at his home.

01:23:26.520 --> 01:23:30.060
Oh! You're here!

01:23:30.060 --> 01:23:32.690
Here's a good sommelier badge for you!

01:23:34.110 --> 01:23:35.780
And for your tastevin!

01:23:35.780 --> 01:23:38.360
Oh! Lookin' sharp!

01:23:43.450 --> 01:23:46.290
You tried to kill Tsuji-<i>san</i> for that?!

01:23:46.290 --> 01:23:51.040
"For that"?! You can't possibly understand how I felt then!

01:23:51.040 --> 01:23:55.460
I sought dignity, honor, and pride as a sommelier in my work!

01:23:55.460 --> 01:23:59.590
And he stomped on all of it with his grimy feet!

01:23:59.590 --> 01:24:02.640
Did you kill Murakami Joe?

01:24:02.640 --> 01:24:04.060
Yeah.

01:24:04.060 --> 01:24:08.100
The day he was released from prison,
I just happened to meet him

01:24:08.100 --> 01:24:10.730
in front of the Mori Detective Agency.

01:24:10.730 --> 01:24:13.940
That's the day he went to play mahjong!

01:24:13.940 --> 01:24:17.360
I thought I might be able to use Murakami,

01:24:17.360 --> 01:24:20.490
so I invited him over as an acquaintance of Mori-<i>san.</i>

01:24:20.490 --> 01:24:24.580
Way back when, he did hold a grudge against Mori-<i>san,</i>

01:24:24.580 --> 01:24:28.790
but now he wanted to apologize for everything, so he went to see him.

01:24:28.790 --> 01:24:32.000
That's when I came up with the idea of using playing card numbers

01:24:32.000 --> 01:24:35.460
to camouflage my crimes.

01:24:35.460 --> 01:24:39.550
Killing Murakami while he was wasted was easy.

01:24:39.550 --> 01:24:43.840
So you had no grudge against Mori-<i>san</i> or Inspector Megure, then?!

01:24:43.840 --> 01:24:44.970
Exactly.

01:24:44.970 --> 01:24:47.560
So you brought me and Shishido-<i>san</i> here...

01:24:47.560 --> 01:24:50.310
...because you needed a "four" and a "six"?!

01:24:50.310 --> 01:24:51.520
That's right.

01:24:51.520 --> 01:24:54.270
I figured three and five-
Mori-<i>san</i> and Detective Shiratori-

01:24:54.270 --> 01:24:59.280
would naturally come if I mentioned
Asahi-<i>san</i> invited me here.

01:24:59.280 --> 01:25:04.410
I had actually hoped "one" -
Kudo Shinichi would come too...

01:25:04.410 --> 01:25:07.120
...but unfortunately, my wish didn't come true.

01:25:07.120 --> 01:25:11.960
Did you ever stop to consider if innocent people were killed?!

01:25:11.960 --> 01:25:16.590
I blew up the underwater restaurant simply to kill Nishina.

01:25:16.590 --> 01:25:20.550
I didn't give a damn whether any of the others lived or died.

01:25:20.550 --> 01:25:24.260
This place would collapse afterward,
Murakami would go missing,

01:25:24.260 --> 01:25:27.560
and it'd all remain an unsolved mystery.

01:25:27.560 --> 01:25:29.850
This place would collapse?!

01:25:29.850 --> 01:25:33.850
Sawaki-<i>san</i>. There's nowhere to run now. Give yourself up.

01:25:33.850 --> 01:25:36.730
Detective Shiratori! Seize Sawaki-<i>san</i>!

01:25:36.730 --> 01:25:37.190
What?!

01:25:43.990 --> 01:25:45.320
W-what the?!

01:25:46.950 --> 01:25:49.080
Oh no!

01:25:49.080 --> 01:25:50.450
Come on!

01:25:50.450 --> 01:25:51.620
Crap!

01:25:54.460 --> 01:25:57.250
Huh? Why does Sawaki-<i>san</i> have Ran?

01:25:57.250 --> 01:26:01.670
What are you talking about?!
You just exposed his crimes!

01:26:01.670 --> 01:26:03.260
Huh? I did?

01:26:04.260 --> 01:26:07.430
Stay where you are! Move and she's dead!

01:26:07.430 --> 01:26:11.270
Damn it! Ran's too out of it to use her karate-

01:26:35.790 --> 01:26:40.380
That last explosion has caused the building to lose its balance!

01:26:40.380 --> 01:26:41.920
Ran! Where are you?!

01:26:41.920 --> 01:26:42.920
Up there!

01:26:42.920 --> 01:26:44.550
Where is he going?!

01:26:44.550 --> 01:26:46.510
He plans to escape in a helicopter!

01:26:46.510 --> 01:26:47.640
What?!

01:26:49.470 --> 01:26:53.350
He called one here using the secretary's name so he could escape!

01:26:53.350 --> 01:26:54.600
That's what he thinks!

01:26:54.600 --> 01:26:57.480
Wait! Mori-<i>kun</i>! Leave the rest to us-

01:26:57.480 --> 01:26:58.520
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:26:58.520 --> 01:27:02.150
--You guys evacuate immediately!
--I-I can't swim!

01:27:02.150 --> 01:27:07.110
Don't worry! We'll find a plank or something and get you to shore!

01:27:07.110 --> 01:27:09.070
--Let's go, Shiratori-<i>kun</i>!
--Yes, sir!

01:27:13.660 --> 01:27:16.330
--Which way?!
--Up the stairs!

01:27:16.330 --> 01:27:18.170
The elevator, huh?!

01:27:26.090 --> 01:27:27.800
Mori-<i>kun</i>! This way!

01:27:29.010 --> 01:27:30.760
Hurry! Hurry!

01:27:43.980 --> 01:27:47.400
Inspector. How good is
Detective Shiratori with a gun?

01:27:47.400 --> 01:27:50.160
He's as bad as I am.

01:27:57.290 --> 01:28:00.460
W-what in the world's going on?!

01:28:03.920 --> 01:28:06.170
What are you doing?! Land!

01:28:06.170 --> 01:28:10.010
W-who is this guy?!
Why does he have a knife?!

01:28:16.350 --> 01:28:20.640
Dammit! Why doesn't that elevator go to the roof?!

01:28:23.020 --> 01:28:27.030
Get down here now!
I'm the one who ordered the chopper!

01:28:27.030 --> 01:28:29.320
Emergency! Emergency!

01:28:29.320 --> 01:28:34.200
A man with a knife has a girl hostage on the Aqua Crystal heliport!

01:28:34.200 --> 01:28:37.580
And the building is in danger of collapsing! Send help at once!

01:28:40.500 --> 01:28:42.790
Ran!

01:28:42.790 --> 01:28:44.000
Stay back!

01:28:44.000 --> 01:28:45.920
Any closer and she's dead!

01:28:45.920 --> 01:28:48.920
Stop this, Sawaki-<i>san</i>!

01:28:48.920 --> 01:28:51.300
Let Ran-<i>san</i> go! Let her go or I'll shoot!

01:28:51.300 --> 01:28:52.680
Amusing!

01:28:52.680 --> 01:28:54.850
Go ahead and shoot, if you dare!

01:28:56.720 --> 01:28:59.850
His hands are shaKing! 
He'll hit Ran if he shoots!

01:28:59.850 --> 01:29:02.770
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>! Don't!

01:29:02.770 --> 01:29:04.770
Inspector! Are you all right?!

01:29:04.770 --> 01:29:08.400
Escaping in a helicopter won't help you! Let Ran-<i>kun</i> go!

01:29:08.400 --> 01:29:11.780
Shut up! I'm gonna take this girl and go kill Tsuji!

01:29:11.780 --> 01:29:13.070
Tsuji-<i>san</i>?!

01:29:13.070 --> 01:29:15.660
He can't be in the
All-American Open now!

01:29:15.660 --> 01:29:17.370
Isn't that enough?!

01:29:17.370 --> 01:29:20.040
Nope! I'm going to kill him, and then I'm going to die!

01:29:20.040 --> 01:29:22.040
And she's coming with me!

01:29:26.250 --> 01:29:29.170
S-Sawaki-<i>san...</i>

01:29:29.170 --> 01:29:32.420
Shinichi... Help me...

01:29:32.420 --> 01:29:34.090
Shinichi...

01:29:34.090 --> 01:29:37.390
If he runs off with Ran, he'll kill her!

01:29:45.560 --> 01:29:50.190
This is bad! If this keeps up, we'll all be goners, not just Ran!

01:29:50.190 --> 01:29:52.030
Hand over the gun.

01:29:52.030 --> 01:29:52.820
What?!

01:29:52.820 --> 01:29:54.660
I'll stab her!

01:29:58.830 --> 01:30:03.000
Hey, Shiratori. Gimme the gun.

01:30:03.000 --> 01:30:05.080
I said give it to me.

01:30:05.080 --> 01:30:08.090
Yeah, right! I can't give it to you!

01:30:08.090 --> 01:30:10.550
What're you doing?! Hurry it up!

01:30:12.130 --> 01:30:13.800
A-all right!

01:30:23.350 --> 01:30:26.810
Boy! You bring it here!

01:30:26.810 --> 01:30:29.610
Do you want this girl to die?!

01:30:29.610 --> 01:30:33.320
N-no! Don't make a kid do something that dangerous!

01:30:33.320 --> 01:30:34.570
Hey!

01:30:39.870 --> 01:30:41.870
C'mon! Bring it here!

01:30:41.870 --> 01:30:44.160
N-no!

01:30:44.160 --> 01:30:47.710
Conan-<i>kun</i>... D-don't give-

01:30:47.710 --> 01:30:50.130
Don't give it to him!

01:30:53.050 --> 01:30:56.590
'Atta boy! Now bring it here!

01:31:02.180 --> 01:31:03.770
Hurry up!

01:31:04.980 --> 01:31:07.190
I said bring it here now!

01:31:09.560 --> 01:31:14.860
Ah! Now I see! That's why the old guy...

01:31:33.800 --> 01:31:35.260
Shi-

01:31:37.380 --> 01:31:39.470
Shinichi?

01:31:51.610 --> 01:31:54.610
Damn it! Hey! Get up! Hey!

01:31:54.610 --> 01:31:56.530
Hey! Hey!

01:31:58.400 --> 01:32:13.170
<i>I sadly watched the rain</i>

01:31:58.400 --> 01:32:13.170
<i>pound on you as you bent over</i>

01:32:07.830 --> 01:32:09.080
Ran!

01:32:13.170 --> 01:32:27.850
<i>If there was only one umbrella in</i>

01:32:13.170 --> 01:32:27.850
<i>this world, I'd find it for you</i>

01:32:16.170 --> 01:32:18.470
That was a close one, Ran...

01:32:18.470 --> 01:32:21.430
N-now I see! So that's why Mori-<i>san</i>

01:32:21.430 --> 01:32:22.430
shot her back then!

01:32:22.430 --> 01:32:24.510
It wasn't to stop the killer,

01:32:24.510 --> 01:32:26.770
but to save the hostage!

01:32:26.770 --> 01:32:29.690
Yes. A hostage shot in the leg

01:32:27.850 --> 01:32:42.450
<i>I can't do anything, but I can't</i>

01:32:27.850 --> 01:32:42.450
<i>get drenched in your place, either</i>

01:32:29.690 --> 01:32:34.570
is just a burden to a fleeing criminal.

01:32:34.570 --> 01:32:37.320
It was to save Mom...

01:32:37.320 --> 01:32:40.530
was the truth, then?

01:32:42.450 --> 01:32:54.710
<i>I beg of you,</i>

01:32:42.450 --> 01:32:54.710
<i>please confess your worries to me</i>

01:32:46.540 --> 01:32:47.870
Sawaki Kohei!

01:32:47.870 --> 01:32:50.040
You're under arrest for murder,

01:32:50.040 --> 01:32:52.250
bodily harm, kidnapping, and more!

01:33:03.390 --> 01:33:05.800
Let go! Let me die!

01:33:08.640 --> 01:33:10.560
I'm not letting you die!

01:33:10.560 --> 01:33:14.770
I'm gonna make you understand the weight of what you've done!

01:33:42.800 --> 01:33:45.550
Talk about a close call!

01:33:45.550 --> 01:33:49.600
It looks like you're over your fear of helicopters now, huh?!

01:33:55.900 --> 01:33:59.070
Let me off this thing!

01:33:59.070 --> 01:34:01.150
Here you go!

01:34:01.150 --> 01:34:04.910
He suddenly jumped at me, so I got surprised!

01:34:04.910 --> 01:34:09.120
Honestly! It's just a good thing you only grazed Ran-<i>san</i>'s leg.

01:34:09.120 --> 01:34:12.290
Anywhere else and things could've ended badly.

01:34:12.290 --> 01:34:14.080
I'm sorry!

01:34:14.080 --> 01:34:18.840
Can't really tell him that my old man often taught me how to shoot

01:34:18.840 --> 01:34:23.590
at the shooting range when we visited the lodge in Hawaii!

01:34:23.590 --> 01:34:27.890
But... I did cause Ran pain...

01:34:29.600 --> 01:34:33.560
Inspector! This is the perfect opportunity to take some time off!

01:34:33.560 --> 01:34:35.940
Yeah, I think I will!

01:34:35.940 --> 01:34:38.230
The hat can stay on, if you don't mind.

01:34:38.230 --> 01:34:42.570
Say, do you think even Shinichi would've shot like you did?

01:34:42.570 --> 01:34:46.950
Who knows. He might've, if he was as good a shot as me.

01:34:46.950 --> 01:34:50.240
I think so, too. Right, Shinichi?

01:34:50.240 --> 01:34:51.700
What's that?

01:34:51.700 --> 01:34:54.660
Shinichi's card. The Ace of Spades.

01:34:54.660 --> 01:34:58.080
I was holding onto it the whole time.

01:34:58.080 --> 01:35:01.920
Who knows, maybe Shinichi helped protect me!

01:35:01.920 --> 01:35:04.720
You dummy! The person saved by the ace...

01:35:04.720 --> 01:35:06.680
"An 'A' is in your future"

01:35:08.760 --> 01:35:10.390
...was me...

01:35:11.260 --> 01:35:12.350
...you know!

01:35:27.450 --> 01:35:32.730
In this repeating dream

01:35:27.450 --> 01:35:32.730
kuri kaeshimiru yume ni

01:35:33.680 --> 01:35:37.900
When I tried to open my eyes

01:35:33.680 --> 01:35:37.900
me ga samete miruto

01:35:39.190 --> 01:35:50.710
I noticed my fast heartbeat

01:35:39.190 --> 01:35:50.710
mune no douki ga hayai koto ni kizuku

01:35:52.450 --> 01:36:03.970
Love does not carve out a rhythm which follows rules

01:35:52.450 --> 01:36:03.970
koi wa kisokutadashi RHYTHM wo kizamanai

01:36:04.130 --> 01:36:16.820
On this comfortable sofa, I fell asleep again

01:36:04.130 --> 01:36:16.820
kokoshi yoi SOFA de nata nemutte shimatta

01:36:19.640 --> 01:36:31.290
Like I've returned to the nostalgic time when I was a teenage girl

01:36:19.640 --> 01:36:31.290
natsukashi shoujo no goro ni modotta mitai ni

01:36:31.450 --> 01:36:37.420
Gently caressing my hair

01:36:31.450 --> 01:36:37.420
yasashiku maki wo nadetekureru

01:36:37.580 --> 01:36:44.430
I've always been awaiting that warm hand

01:36:37.580 --> 01:36:44.430
sonna atatakai te wo itsumo matte ita

01:36:44.710 --> 01:37:01.650
Only you will gently embrace me

01:36:44.710 --> 01:37:01.650
anata dake wa watashi wo sotto tsutsumi kon dekureru

01:37:01.810 --> 01:37:13.420
I love you so much, I love you so much

01:37:01.810 --> 01:37:13.420
totemo aishiteru totemo aishiteru

01:37:40.390 --> 01:37:57.750
Only you will gently embrace me

01:37:40.390 --> 01:37:57.750
anata dake wa watashi wo sotto tsutsumi kon dekureru

01:37:57.910 --> 01:38:10.890
I love you so much, in my red heart

01:37:57.910 --> 01:38:10.890
totemo aishiteru akai HEART de

01:38:11.480 --> 01:38:16.110
Lovin' you

01:38:11.480 --> 01:38:16.110
LOVIN' YOU

01:38:17.660 --> 01:38:22.620
With you

01:38:17.660 --> 01:38:22.620
anata to

01:38:29.960 --> 01:38:33.470
Eh? You knew why Dad shot you?!

01:38:33.470 --> 01:38:37.140
Of course I did! We are married, after all.

01:38:37.140 --> 01:38:41.930
Plus it's only natural for a husband to protect his wife.

01:38:41.930 --> 01:38:44.850
Then why did you leave him?

01:38:47.440 --> 01:38:52.320
That very night, he said my cooking was horrible and didn't eat it.

01:38:52.320 --> 01:38:53.740
Huh?

01:38:53.740 --> 01:38:58.370
My leg hurt so much, and I worked so hard to thank him with food...

01:38:58.370 --> 01:38:59.990
Yet, he...

01:39:01.330 --> 01:39:06.330
You idiot! If this is the best you can make, get the hell to bed!

01:39:06.330 --> 01:39:08.880
And that's why I moved out.

01:39:10.000 --> 01:39:12.170
Just remembering it makes me mad!

01:39:12.170 --> 01:39:14.130
That insensitive old clod!

01:39:14.130 --> 01:39:17.380
O-oh, I see...

01:39:17.380 --> 01:39:20.430
Looks like they won't be making up for a while now...

01:39:20.430 --> 01:39:23.310
Come to think of it, Mom's cooking...

01:39:25.020 --> 01:39:27.190
...was horrible...
